        openings: ("A hotel pool closes at ten each night, and the pool camera shows {D} swimming after closing. A month earlier, {D.he} had been told not to come back, and The court file shows {DL} here in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says a hotel guest invited {D.him} to swim, and {D.he} went along. The defense will show a foolish decision, not a person who sneaked in to cause harm."),
        closings: ("The camera shows {D} swimming after closing, a month after being warned not to return. No guest vouches for {D.him}. {DL} stood in this court once before, in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}. Being told no once is enough.", "A guest invited {DL} to swim, and {D.he} said yes without thinking. {D.He} has promised to stay out of pools after hours and to apologize to the hotel."),
        timeline: [(-30, "Hotel staff warn {D} not to enter the pool area after closing."), (0, "11 p.m.: the pool camera shows {D} swimming after closing."), (0, "11:20 p.m.: the night clerk calls deputies.")],
