        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about your job.", "\"I'm the garage manager at the hospital. I oversee parking passes, collect fees and handle complaints about the garage.\""), .direct("How do you issue passes?", "\"Each pass has a unique serial number, and we keep a log. Staff passes are renewed every quarter and signed out at my office.\""), .direct("What did you find?", "\"Three passes on three different cars, all with the same serial number. That's impossible for genuine passes.\""), .direct("What did the passes look like?", "\"They looked real at a glance, but the print was fuzzy and the hologram was missing. They were printed on regular card stock.\""), .direct("How did you trace them?", "\"The cars belonged to {D} and two coworkers. A printer was found at {DL}'s workstation that matched the print.\""), .direct("What did it cost the hospital?", "\"We lose parking fees for every fake pass. Over several months, that's a few hundred dollars.\""), .cross("Did you find {DL}'s fingerprints on the fake passes?", "\"We didn't test for fingerprints.\""), .cross("Did the other two drivers say where they got their passes?", "\"One said a coworker gave them out. I don't know who.\""), .cross("Was the printer at {DL}'s desk used for other work?", "\"Yes, it was a shared printer used for ordinary documents.\""), .cross("Did {DL} have a valid pass of {D.his} own?", "\"{D.He} had one, but it had expired.\""), .cross("Did {DL} cooperate?", "\"Yes. {D.He} told me where {D.he} got the passes and gave me the coworker's name.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} made fake garage passes for a hospital, three with the same serial number.", "A coworker gave {DL} the passes, and {D.he} used them without knowing they were fake."),
