        truths: ("A printer sat on {DL}'s desk at work, and all three passes had the same serial number.", "The coworker who gave {DL} the passes is real and has been identified."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you make the garage passes?", "\"No. I didn't make any of them, but I used one, and I shouldn't have.\""), .direct("Where did you get the pass?", "\"A coworker gave me three, and told me it was a favor to help with the parking costs.\""), .direct("Who is the coworker?", "\"A man from my department who handed them out as a favor. I gave his name and number to the garage manager and to the deputies.\""), .direct("Why did you use it?", "\"My own pass had run out, and renewing it was expensive. I didn't look at it closely.\""), .direct("Why was there a printer at your desk?", "\"It's the department printer. Everyone uses it, and it was there before I started.\""), .direct("What do you plan to do?", "\"I'll pay the hospital what I owe for parking and use a valid pass from now on.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I know it's a pattern. I should have known better.\""), .cross("You noticed that the pass looked odd, didn't you?", "\"A little. I didn't think it was a forgery, but I should have asked.\""), .cross("You didn't buy the pass from the hospital, did you?", "\"No. I got it from a coworker.\""), .cross("Your coworker isn't here to say he gave it to you, is he?", "\"No, he isn't here, but the hospital and the deputies both have his name and number.\""), .cross("The pass had the same serial number as two others, didn't it?", "\"I didn't know that until later.\"")],
        openings: ("A hospital garage manager found three parking passes with the same serial number, which is impossible for genuine passes. A printer was found at {D}'s desk, and {DL} stood in this court once before, in {PRIORDATE} when the case concerned {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says a coworker gave {D.him} the passes, and {D.he} used them without checking where they came from. The coworker is real, and the defense will show that {D.he} did not make them."),
        closings: ("Three passes, one serial number, and a printer at {D}'s desk. {DL} already has a history in this court, dating to {PRIORDATE} in a case for {PRIOR}. The hospital lost parking revenue to fake passes.", "A coworker handed {D} the passes, and the coworker has been identified. {DL} used them but did not forge them, and the State has not shown {D.he} made a single one."),
        timeline: [(-30, "Fake garage passes begin to appear on cars at the hospital."), (0, "The garage manager notices three passes with the same serial number."), (1, "Deputies find a printer at {D}'s workstation and trace the passes.")],
        identified: "Fake Passes",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let fakeDoctorLetter = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.fakeDoctorLetter",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Worker Hands Supervisor Forged Clinic Letter"],
        law: "uttering",
        spec: "Uttered a forged clinic letter to {V}, an employer, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} gave an employer a forged clinic letter.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Clinic Letter", "The clinic denies it.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Sick", "{DL} says {D.he} was sick.")],
        role: "Shift supervisor",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about your job.", "\"I'm a shift supervisor at a distribution center. I manage the schedule, approve time off and handle attendance issues for about thirty workers.\""), .direct("What did {D} give you?", "\"A letter on clinic letterhead, saying {DL} had been seen and should be excused from work for two days.\""), .direct("Why did you call the clinic?", "\"The signature looked odd, and the date didn't match when {DL} had called out. I called to confirm.\""), .direct("What did the clinic say?", "\"That they had no record of a visit that day, and that the signature and the letterhead were not theirs.\""), .direct("What did you do next?", "\"I told my manager and reported it to the deputies. {DL} was suspended while it was looked into.\""), .direct("Why does the letter matter to the company?", "\"A doctor's note means an excused absence with no penalty. A false one is a way of avoiding discipline.\""), .cross("Had {DL} called out sick before?", "\"Occasionally. {D.He} had a decent attendance record.\""), .cross("Did {DL} say where the letter came from?", "\"{D.He} said a friend had given it to {D.him}.\""), .cross("Did {DL} seem sick when {D.he} returned?", "\"Yes. {D.He} looked pale, and {D.he} coughed through most of the shift.\""), .cross("Did {DL} offer to bring a different note?", "\"{D.He} said {D.he} would get a proper one from the clinic.\""), .cross("Did you see a pharmacy slip from {DL}?", "\"The deputy mentioned one. I haven't seen it myself.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} gave an employer a forged clinic letter to cover an absence.", "{DL} was really sick and used a letter a friend had, without knowing it was not from the clinic."),
        allocution: "\"I was sick, and I gave my employer a letter that wasn't from my clinic, one a friend had. I've been in this courtroom before, and I know that was wrong. I'll apologize to my boss and get a proper note next time.\"",
        truths: ("The clinic denies issuing the letter, and no visit is recorded for that day.", "A pharmacy slip shows {DL} bought medicine that day, which supports the illness."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you give your employer a letter that wasn't from the clinic?", "\"Yes, I did. I was sick, and I gave my supervisor a letter that a friend had.\""), .direct("Why did you use your friend's letter?", "\"I couldn't get an appointment, and I knew the company wanted a note. My friend said it would do.\""), .direct("Were you sick that day?", "\"Yes. I had a fever and a bad cough. I bought medicine at a pharmacy that afternoon.\""), .direct("Did you know it wasn't from your clinic?", "\"I knew it wasn't from my own clinic. I thought my friend's clinic would count, which was a mistake.\""), .direct("Did you try to deceive your supervisor?", "\"I didn't think of it that way. I wanted to show I'd been sick, and I made a poor choice.\""), .direct("What will you do now?", "\"I'll apologize to my boss and get a proper note next time.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I know that was wrong. I should have just told the truth.\""), .cross("The clinic says it didn't issue the letter, doesn't it?", "\"That's what they say, and I believe them.\""), .cross("You handed the letter to your supervisor, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I did hand it over, and I did it without checking the letter at all.\""), .cross("You never visited the clinic that day, did you?", "\"No, I didn't see anyone at the clinic that day, because I couldn't get an appointment.\""), .cross("You could have called the clinic yourself, couldn't you?", "\"I could have phoned the clinic myself that same morning, and I wish I had done exactly that.\"")],
        openings: ("A shift supervisor received a clinic letter excusing {D} from work, and the clinic says it never wrote it. No visit is recorded, and {DL} was in front of this court earlier, in {PRIORDATE} after being charged with {PRIOR}.", "{DL} was sick and handed in a letter a friend had given {D.him}. {D.He} was ill that day, a pharmacy slip shows it, and the defense will show that the absence was real."),
        closings: ("The clinic denies the letter, and no visit is recorded. {D} gave a forged letter to an employer. {DL} has appeared in this courtroom before, back in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}.", "{D} was sick that day, and a pharmacy slip shows medicine. {D.He} used a letter a friend had without checking it. The State has not shown {D.he} knew it was a forgery."),
        timeline: [(0, "Morning: {D} calls out sick from work."), (1, "{D} hands the shift supervisor a clinic letter."), (2, "The supervisor calls the clinic, which denies the letter.")],
        identified: "Clinic Letter",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let churchBakeSale = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.churchBakeSale",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Church Bake Sale Box Taken"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole property of {V}, a church, valued at $260, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} took a cash box from a church bake sale.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Hall Camera", "{D} walks off with a box.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Safe", "{DL} says {D.he} moved it to a safe.")],
        role: "Church volunteer",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about your role at the church.", "\"I'm a volunteer at the church. I help with the monthly bake sale by working the tables and counting the money at the end.\""), .direct("What happened at the bake sale that day?", "\"A few of us stepped away from the table for a few minutes to help with a delivery, and when I came back, the cash box was gone.\""), .direct("What was in the box?", "\"About $260 in cash from the morning's sales. We were saving it for the children's program at the church.\""), .direct("What does the hall camera show?", "\"{D} walks up to the table, looks around, picks up the box and walks out of the hall with it.\""), .direct("Did {DL} tell anyone about taking the box?", "\"Nobody. We didn't know who had it until we looked at the camera, and by then {D.he} was gone.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"We looked all over the hall, and then we called the sheriff's office and gave them what we saw.\""), .cross("Was the table unattended when {DL} took the box?", "\"For a few minutes, yes. We had gone to help carry in a delivery from the church van.\""), .cross("Does the church have a safe?", "\"No. We usually keep the box with a volunteer, and that's why it's so unusual for it to be left alone.\""), .cross("Was the box recovered?", "\"Deputies found it in {D.his} car, and every dollar was still in it.\""), .cross("Did {DL} say why {D.he} took it?", "\"{D.He} said {D.he} was trying to keep it safe, and I can understand how someone might say that.\""), .cross("Is {DL} a member of your church?", "\"Not that I know of. I'd never seen {D.him} before the bake sale.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} lifted a cash box from an unattended bake sale table and walked out of the church hall with it.", "{DL} moved the box to {D.his} car to keep the money safe, and meant to bring it back."),
        allocution: "\"I moved that cash box to my car to keep it safe, and I meant to bring it back. I'll make sure the church gets every dollar.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} left the hall with the box and put it in {D.his} car, and the church has no safe.", "The table had been left unattended and {DL} wanted to protect the money from someone else taking it."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take the cash box from the bake sale table?", "\"Yes, I did. I moved it to my car to keep it safe, and I meant to bring it back.\""), .direct("Why did you think it needed to be kept safe?", "\"The table was empty, and the box was sitting out in the open with people walking by. I worried someone else would take it.\""), .direct("Why didn't you tell a volunteer?", "\"I looked around for someone and couldn't find a soul. I should have waited at the table until somebody came back.\""), .direct("Why did you put it in your car?", "\"I thought it would be safer in my car, and I meant to return in a few minutes. Then I got a phone call and was delayed.\""), .direct("Was all the money still in the box when the deputies came?", "\"Yes, every dollar. I never opened it, and I told them where it was the moment they asked.\""), .direct("What will you do for the church?", "\"I'll make sure the church gets every dollar, and I'll apologize to the volunteers in person for the worry I caused.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, I was here before, and I can see how this looks to the volunteers. I'm sorry for the worry I caused them.\""), .cross("You took the box without asking anyone, didn't you?", "\"I did. I should have found a volunteer first, and I'm sorry I didn't.\""), .cross("You walked out of the hall with the box, didn't you?", "\"Yes, and the camera shows it. I don't dispute any of that.\""), .cross("There is no safe at the church, is there?", "\"No. I realize now I should have just left the box where it was and gone to find someone.\""), .cross("You didn't call anyone to say you had it, did you?", "\"No, and I should have. I meant to, but I never did.\"")],
        openings: ("A church bake sale had a cash box on its table, and the hall camera shows {D} lifting it and walking out. The box held $260 for the children's program. Court records have {DL} here before, in {PRIORDATE} in a case for {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says the table was unattended, and {D.he} picked up the box to keep it safe and meant to bring it back. The defense will show that every dollar was in the box when deputies found it in {D.his} car."),
        closings: ("The hall camera shows {D} lifting the church's cash box and walking out of the building. The money was for the children's program. {DL} was last before this court in {PRIORDATE} in the case known as {PRIOR}. The box was not {D}'s to move.", "The table was left unattended, and {D} moved the box to protect it, meaning to bring it back. Every dollar was in it when deputies found it. {DL} has promised that the church will have every dollar."),
        timeline: [(0, "Saturday morning: the church bake sale runs in the fellowship hall."), (0, "Midday: volunteers step away, and {D} lifts the cash box and walks out."), (0, "Afternoon: the volunteers find the box missing and call deputies.")],
        identified: "Hall Camera",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let motelLamps = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.motelLamps",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Guest Walks Out With Motel Bedding and Lamp"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole property of {V}, a motel, valued at $310, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} left a motel with bedding and a lamp.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Lobby Camera", "{D} carries a bundle.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Told", "{DL} says staff said to take them.")],
        role: "Motel clerk",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about your job at the motel.", "\"I'm a clerk at the motel. I check guests in and out, take payments, and answer calls from the rooms.\""), .direct("What happened when {D} checked out?", "\"{DL} came to the desk, handed back the key and walked out through the lobby carrying a large bundle wrapped in a blanket.\""), .direct("What was missing from the room?", "\"The comforter, two sheets, the pillowcases and the bedside lamp. All together, the replacement cost was about $310.\""), .direct("What does the lobby camera show?", "\"{DL} walking out the front doors with a bundle under one arm and the lamp in the other hand, in plain view of the desk.\""), .direct("Did anyone at the motel give {DL} permission to take those items?", "\"Not that I know of. I asked every staff member on duty that morning, and nobody remembers saying anything like that.\""), .direct("What did you do about it?", "\"Housekeeping told me what was missing, and I reviewed the camera. Then I called the sheriff's office and gave them the footage.\""), .cross("Did {DL} try to hide the items as {D.he} left?", "\"Not really. {D.He} carried them openly through the lobby, in front of the desk, and didn't hurry.\""), .cross("Did {DL} say anything to you at checkout?", "\"{D.He} said something about being told to take them. I didn't hear it clearly, and I didn't think much of it then.\""), .cross("Was the lamp returned?", "\"Yes. {D.He} brought it back a few days later and left it at the front desk.\""), .cross("Have the bedding items been returned?", "\"Not as of now. {D.He} has said {D.he} would bring them back, but I haven't seen them.\""), .cross("Has {DL} stayed at your motel before?", "\"Yes, a couple of times, and I never heard of any problem.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} carried bedding and a bedside lamp out of a motel room at checkout.", "Staff told {DL} {D.he} could take the bedding and the lamp, and {D.he} returned the lamp when {D.he} realized there might be a problem."),
        allocution: "\"I thought the motel staff said I could take the bedding and the lamp, and I left with them. I've been in this courtroom before, and I know I should have asked for it in writing. I'll return everything or pay for it.\"",
        truths: ("No staff member remembers giving that instruction, and the lobby camera shows {DL} walking out with a bundle.", "The lamp came back within days, which shows {DL} never meant to keep it."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take the bedding and the lamp from the motel room?", "\"Yes, I did. I thought a staff member had told me I could take them, and I left with them.\""), .direct("Who told you that?", "\"A woman at the front desk, when I asked about the old bedding. I thought she said it was fine to take it.\""), .direct("Why did you carry the items out in the open?", "\"Because I believed they were mine to take. If I'd thought it was wrong, I'd have hidden them.\""), .direct("What did you do with the lamp?", "\"I brought it back a few days later, when I realized there might be a problem and wanted to fix it.\""), .direct("Where is the bedding now?", "\"It's at my place, and I'll bring it back or pay for it. I never meant to keep anything I wasn't supposed to.\""), .direct("Why didn't you ask for something in writing?", "\"I should have. I thought a verbal okay at the desk was good enough, and I didn't think any more about it.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I know I should have asked for it in writing. I'm sorry for the trouble this caused.\""), .cross("You can't name the staff member who told you, can you?", "\"No, I don't know her name. She was behind the desk, and I'd never asked.\""), .cross("Nobody at the motel remembers saying that, do they?", "\"That's what I've been told. I understand why that makes it look different.\""), .cross("You left without paying for the items, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I thought they were free, but I know that doesn't help me now.\""), .cross("You returned the lamp only after the deputies got involved, didn't you?", "\"That's true, and I'm sorry it took that long. I should have gone back at once.\"")],
        openings: ("A motel clerk found a room stripped of its comforter, sheets, pillowcases and a bedside lamp, and the lobby camera shows {D} carrying a bundle out. The items were worth $310. {DL} came through this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says a staff member told {D.him} that {D.he} could take the old bedding and the lamp when {D.he} left, and {D.he} carried them out openly. The defense will show that {D.he} returned the lamp and has offered to return the rest."),
        closings: ("The lobby camera shows {D} carrying a bundle out of the motel, and the room was missing its bedding and a lamp. No one at the motel remembers telling {D.him} to take anything. {DL} was in front of this court earlier, in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}.", "{D} walked through the lobby in plain view, believing staff had said the items were {D.his} to take. {D.He} brought the lamp back and has offered to return or pay for the rest. That is a mistake about permission, not a theft."),
        timeline: [(0, "Morning: {D} checks out of the motel room and returns the key."), (0, "The lobby camera shows {D} carrying a large bundle and a lamp out the front doors."), (0, "Housekeeping finds the room stripped of bedding and a lamp.")],
        identified: "Lobby Camera",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let karaokeAgain = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.karaokeAgain",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Man Hurls Chair at Karaoke Night"],
        law: "disorderly",
        spec: "Disturbed the peace of {V}, a bar, by violent conduct, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} threw a chair at a second bar's karaoke night.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Bar Camera", "{D} throws a chair.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Drunk", "{DL} says {D.he} was drunk.")],
        role: "Bar manager",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about your job at the bar.", "\"I'm the manager of the bar. I supervise the bartenders, handle disputes between customers and make sure we follow the rules on serving alcohol.\""), .direct("What happened during karaoke night that evening?", "\"At about eleven, {D} stood up from a table, lifted a chair with both hands and threw it across the room. It was loud and everyone froze.\""), .direct("What does the bar camera show?", "\"It shows {DL} rising from the table, swaying a little, then throwing the chair toward the stage area, where it hit a speaker stand.\""), .direct("Was anyone hurt?", "\"No. People ran out of the way, and the chair landed near the stage. A speaker stand broke, and we had to stop the music for a while.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I told {DL} to leave and called the sheriff's office. {D.He} was angry at first but left when I asked.\""), .direct("How much had {DL} been drinking?", "\"I'm told several drinks over about two hours. I wasn't watching {D.him} personally, but the bartenders' tab shows a steady stream.\""), .cross("Did your staff keep serving {DL} after {D.he} appeared drunk?", "\"I'd have to check with the bartender who was on. I know that {D.he} was served right up until the chair.\""), .cross("Does your license require you to stop serving visibly intoxicated customers?", "\"Yes, it does. That's one of the conditions of our permit, and we train the staff on it.\""), .cross("Was the chair thrown at a particular person?", "\"It was thrown toward the stage, not at anyone that I could see on the camera.\""), .cross("Did {DL} apologize?", "\"Yes, later that night, through a friend, who also offered to pay for the stand.\""), .cross("Have you heard that {DL} was banned from another bar?", "\"I've heard that, yes, but I don't know the details.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} threw a chair across a crowded bar during karaoke night after drinking heavily.", "{DL} was drunk and acted without thinking, and the bar had kept serving {D.him} well past the point when {D.he} should have been cut off."),
        allocution: "\"I'd been drinking, and I threw a chair at that karaoke night, and I'm ashamed. I've been in this courtroom before for something similar. I'll pay for any damage and I'll stay out of bars until I get a handle on this.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had already been banned from another bar for similar behavior, and the camera shows the chair leave {D.his} hands.", "The bar served {DL} drink after drink even though {D.he} was clearly intoxicated."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you throw the chair at karaoke night?", "\"Yes, I did, and I'm ashamed of it. I'd been drinking for hours, and I lost control.\""), .direct("How much had you been drinking?", "\"A lot, over several hours. I wasn't counting, and the bar kept bringing me more, which I didn't turn down.\""), .direct("Why did you throw the chair?", "\"I was upset about something that had happened earlier, and the drinks took away my judgment. I didn't aim at anyone.\""), .direct("Did anyone try to stop you?", "\"A friend tried to calm me down and take my arm, and I brushed him off. I wish I'd listened to him.\""), .direct("What happened after you threw it?", "\"The room went quiet. I sat down for a second, and then the manager told me to go, and I left.\""), .direct("What do you plan to do?", "\"I'll pay for any damage, and I'll stay out of bars until I get a handle on my drinking. I'm going to ask my doctor about help.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before for something similar, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I promised myself it wouldn't happen again. I let myself and everyone else down.\""), .cross("You could have hurt someone with that chair, couldn't you?", "\"Yes, I could have. I'm lucky that nobody was hit, and I think about that every day.\""), .cross("You were banned from another bar for this kind of thing, weren't you?", "\"Yes, for something similar. That should have been the end of it, and I'm ashamed it wasn't.\""), .cross("Nobody forced you to keep drinking that night, did they?", "\"No. I kept ordering, and I take responsibility for that, even if the bar should have stopped me.\""), .cross("The bar never cut you off, did it?", "\"Not that I recall. That doesn't excuse what I did, but it's part of how the night went.\"")],
        openings: ("On karaoke night, a bar camera shows {D} lift a chair and hurl it across a crowded room, and patrons scattered. The chair broke a speaker stand and landed near the stage. {DL} has appeared in this courtroom before, back in {PRIORDATE} when the case concerned {PRIOR}.", "{DL} admits that {D.he} had too much to drink and acted without thinking. The defense will show that the bar kept serving {D.him} long after {D.he} was drunk, and that {D.he} threw the chair toward the stage, not at a person."),
        closings: ("A chair flew across a crowded bar, and the camera shows {D} throwing it. People scattered, and a speaker stand broke. This is not {DL}'s first time here, since {PRIORDATE} brought {D.him} in once already when the case concerned {PRIOR}. Violence in a public place disturbs the peace, drunk or not.", "{D} admits to drinking too much, and the bar kept pouring. The chair went toward the stage and no person was hit. {DL} has said that {D.he} will pay for the damage and stay out of bars until {D.he} gets help."),
        timeline: [(0, "9 p.m.: karaoke night begins and {D} is served several drinks."), (0, "11 p.m.: {D} lifts a chair and throws it across the room toward the stage."), (0, "11:05 p.m.: the manager tells {D} to leave and calls deputies.")],
        identified: "Bar Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let hydrantAgain = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.hydrantAgain",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Hydrant Opened Again in Hot Weather"],
        law: "injuryRealProperty",
        spec: "Willfully and wantonly injured real property of {V}, a town, causing damage of $900, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} opened a hydrant on a hot day.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Street Camera", "{D} turns the valve.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Heat", "{DL} says it was hot.")],
        role: "Public works supervisor",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about your job with the town.", "\"I'm a supervisor with the town's public works department. I manage the crews who maintain our streets, water lines and hydrants.\""), .direct("What was reported that afternoon?", "\"A neighbor called to say a hydrant was running wide open on a residential street, flooding the road and a neighbor's yard.\""), .direct("What did you find when you arrived?", "\"The valve had been stripped, so we couldn't close the hydrant the normal way. We had to shut off the main for the whole block.\""), .direct("What does the street camera show?", "\"It shows {D} with a long wrench, opening the hydrant, and a big stream of water coming out across the street.\""), .direct("What did the repair cost the town?", "\"Replacing the valve and the cap, plus labor and the lost water, came to about $900.\""), .direct("Why is it a problem when someone opens a hydrant?", "\"It drops the water pressure for the neighborhood, and a fire crew could have trouble getting enough water if a fire broke out.\""), .cross("Was the hydrant old?", "\"It was about thirty years old. Some of the valves in that part of town are worn, and they get stiff.\""), .cross("Do you know whether {DL} meant to break the valve?", "\"I can't say. The wrench {D.he} used was the right kind, but the valve stripped as {D.he} forced it.\""), .cross("Did {DL} stay at the scene?", "\"Yes. {D.He} stayed and helped us close off the street, and {D.he} was upset about the water.\""), .cross("Was anyone hurt?", "\"No. The street flooded a bit and a yard got soaked, but nobody was injured.\""), .cross("Has the hydrant been repaired?", "\"Yes, my crew replaced the valve that same week, and it's working normally now.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} opened a town fire hydrant with a wrench on a very hot day and stripped the valve.", "It was sweltering, and {DL} opened the hydrant to cool the street without thinking about the damage."),
        allocution: "\"It was hot, and I opened the hydrant to cool the street down, and I didn't think about the water. I've been in this courtroom before about the same hydrant. I'll help pay and leave it alone from now on.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} used a wrench that stripped the valve, and the repair cost the town $900.", "The valve stripped because it was old and worn, and {DL} never meant to break it."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you open the hydrant?", "\"Yes, I did. It was a very hot day, and I wanted to cool the street off. I didn't think about what it would do.\""), .direct("Why did you use a wrench?", "\"It's the only way to open a hydrant, and I had one in my truck. I've seen crews use the same kind of wrench.\""), .direct("Did you mean to break the valve?", "\"No. It was stiff, and I forced it, and then it stripped. I never meant for it to be damaged.\""), .direct("What did you do when the water started?", "\"I tried to close it, and I couldn't. I called the town right away when I saw that it wouldn't shut.\""), .direct("Why did you open it?", "\"I wasn't thinking. Kids were outside on the street, and it was ninety-five degrees. It seemed like a harmless way to cool everyone down.\""), .direct("How will you make it right?", "\"I'll help pay for the repair, and I'll leave hydrants alone from now on. I'm sorry for the trouble.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before about the same hydrant, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I promised myself I wouldn't do it again. I'm embarrassed that I'm back here.\""), .cross("You knew it was town property, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I knew. I should have known better than to touch it.\""), .cross("Hydrants are meant for fire crews, aren't they?", "\"Yes, and I know that now. I should have thought about what it would mean if a fire broke out.\""), .cross("The damage came to $900, didn't it?", "\"That's what the town says, and I'll help pay. I don't dispute the amount.\""), .cross("You didn't ask the town for permission, did you?", "\"No, I didn't. I should have called and asked whether there was a way to cool the street safely.\"")],
        openings: ("On a ninety-five degree afternoon, a street camera shows {D} using a long wrench to open a town hydrant. The valve stripped, water flooded the street, and the repair cost $900. {DL} returns to this court having been here in {PRIORDATE} after being charged with {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says it was brutally hot, and {D.he} opened the hydrant to cool the street without thinking about the water. The defense will show a foolish act on a sweltering day, and a valve that was already thirty years old."),
        closings: ("The street camera shows {D} turning a hydrant valve with a wrench, and the valve stripped. The town paid $900 to repair it and lost water for the block. {DL} came through this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}. Opening a hydrant is not a harmless prank.", "It was ninety-five degrees, and {D} wanted to cool the street for the kids. The valve was old and worn. {DL} never meant to break it and has promised to help pay for the repair."),
        timeline: [(0, "Afternoon: the temperature reaches ninety-five degrees on a residential street."), (0, "{D} opens the hydrant with a wrench and the valve strips."), (0, "Public works arrives, shuts off the main for the block and starts the repair.")],
        identified: "Street Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let tennisCourtSkate = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.tennisCourtSkate",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Skaters Use Closed Tennis Court"],
        law: "trespass2",
        spec: "Entered and remained on the premises of {V}, a town park, after being notified not to, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} skated a closed court and damaged the net.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Park Camera", "{D} skates inside.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "No Signs", "{DL} says no signs were visible.")],
        role: "Park ranger",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about your work for the town.", "\"I'm a park ranger for the town. I patrol the parks every day, enforce the posted rules, and respond to damage and complaints.\""), .direct("What was the status of the tennis court that week?", "\"It was closed for resurfacing for several days. A contractor had applied a new coating, and we tied closure signs to the fence at both gates.\""), .direct("What did you see when you arrived at the court?", "\"I saw {D} on skates, riding back and forth across the court. The gate was open and nobody else was on the surface.\""), .direct("What damage did you find?", "\"The net had been pulled down at one end, and the fresh coating had scuff marks and a few deep scratches from the skates.\""), .direct("What does the park camera show?", "\"It shows {DL} entering through the gate, skating several laps, and the net catching on a skate and being dragged down.\""), .direct("What did you do about it?", "\"I told {DL} to leave the court, took a statement and wrote a report. The contractor later gave us a repair estimate for the coating and the net.\""), .cross("Were the closure signs visible to someone standing at the gate?", "\"Most of them were. One had fallen off the fence, and I believe another was partly hidden behind a branch.\""), .cross("Did {DL} argue with you when you asked {D.him} to leave?", "\"No. {D.He} said {D.he} had not seen any signs, and {D.he} stopped skating right away and apologized.\""), .cross("Was the gate locked that day?", "\"No, the gate was open. We'd left it open for the contractor earlier and it hadn't been closed.\""), .cross("Did {DL} offer to pay for the damage to the net?", "\"Yes, {D.he} offered to pay as soon as I told {D.him} what it would cost.\""), .cross("Had you warned {DL} about this court before?", "\"I'd spoken to {D.him} once about another area of the park, but never about this court.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} skated across a town tennis court that was closed for resurfacing and damaged the net.", "No closure signs were visible at the gate, and {DL} believed the court was open."),
        allocution: "\"I didn't see any sign on that tennis court, and I skated on it. I damaged the net, and I'll pay for it. I've been in this courtroom before, and I'll check every gate before I go in.\"",
        truths: ("Closure signs were zip-tied to the fence at both gates, and {DL}'s skates caught the net.", "One sign had fallen to the ground and another was hidden behind a branch, so {DL} never saw either."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you skate on the closed tennis court?", "\"Yes, I did. I didn't see any sign, and I thought the court was open, so I went in through the gate.\""), .direct("How did you get onto the court?", "\"I walked through the gate, which was standing open. I didn't climb a fence or move anything to get in.\""), .direct("Did you see any closure signs?", "\"No. One was on the ground by the fence, and another was behind a branch. I walked right past without noticing either.\""), .direct("How did the net get damaged?", "\"My skate caught the bottom of the net while I was turning, and it pulled the whole thing down at one end. I didn't mean to hurt it.\""), .direct("What did you do when the ranger arrived?", "\"I stopped right away and apologized. I told him I hadn't seen any signs, and I offered to pay for the net.\""), .direct("What will you do from now on?", "\"I'll check every gate and fence before I go onto any court, and I'll pay for the damage I caused.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I know I should have been more careful. I'm not asking to be excused from the damage.\""), .cross("You skated on a freshly coated surface, didn't you?", "\"I did. I could see afterward that I'd left marks on it, and I felt terrible about that.\""), .cross("The ranger had spoken to you about another part of the park before, hadn't he?", "\"Yes, once, about a different spot. That's why I should have been watching more closely this time.\""), .cross("You could have asked someone whether the court was open, couldn't you?", "\"I could have asked, but there was nobody around, so I just walked in without thinking about it.\""), .cross("There were closure signs on the fence, weren't there?", "\"So I've been told, and I accept that. I honestly didn't see them that day.\"")],
        openings: ("A town park closed its tennis court for resurfacing and tied signs to the fence, and the park camera shows {D} skating on the new surface. The net was pulled down and the coating was scuffed. {DL} came through this court in {PRIORDATE} when the case concerned {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says no sign was visible from the gate, and the court looked open, so {D.he} skated on it. The defense will show that one sign had fallen and another was hidden, and that {DL} has offered to pay for the net."),
        closings: ("The court was closed, the signs were on the fence, and the camera shows {D} skating on a fresh surface and pulling down the net. {DL} returns to this court having been here in {PRIORDATE} in the case known as {PRIOR}. A closed court is closed, whatever a person thinks.", "A sign was lying on the ground and another was behind a branch. {D} saw nothing telling {D.him} to stay out, and {D.he} stopped when the ranger spoke. {DL} has offered to pay for the net and will check every gate from now on."),
        timeline: [(-3, "The town closes the tennis court for resurfacing and zip-ties signs to the fence."), (0, "Afternoon: {D} enters through the open gate and skates across the new surface."), (0, "{D}'s skates catch the net, and a park ranger arrives and tells {D.him} to leave.")],
        identified: "Park Camera",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let daycareFenceLoiter = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.daycareFenceLoiter",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Man Lingers at Day Care Fence After Warning"],
        law: "trespass2",
        spec: "Entered and remained on the premises of {V}, a day care, after being notified not to, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} stood by a day care fence after a warning.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Day Care Camera", "{D} stands by the fence.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Waiting", "{DL} says {D.he} waited for a niece.")],
        role: "Director",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about your role at the day care.", "\"I'm the director of the day care. I'm responsible for the children's safety, the staff, and making sure children go home only with approved adults.\""), .direct("Why did you warn {D} earlier?", "\"I'd seen {DL} standing at the playground fence watching the children, and I didn't know who {D.he} was. I told {D.him} to stay away from the fence.\""), .direct("What did the camera show on the day you called deputies?", "\"It showed {DL} back at the same fence, standing for about twenty minutes and looking toward the playground while the children were outside.\""), .direct("Is {DL} on any approved pickup list?", "\"No. {D.He} isn't on any list, and none of the parents had told us to expect {D.him}.\""), .direct("What did you do when you saw {D.him}?", "\"I brought the children inside right away and called the sheriff's office. I wasn't going to take a chance with a stranger at the fence.\""), .direct("Why do you control who stands near the fence?", "\"Parents trust us to know who is near their children. We can't have strangers watching the playground, whatever the reason.\""), .cross("Have you learned that one of {DL}'s relatives attends the day care?", "\"Yes. I've since learned that a niece of {D.his} is enrolled, though I hadn't known it at the time.\""), .cross("Did {DL} speak to any child or try to open the gate?", "\"No. {D.He} stayed on the sidewalk side of the fence the whole time and didn't touch anything.\""), .cross("Did {DL} threaten you or the staff?", "\"No. {D.He} was polite when I spoke to {D.him}, and {D.he} left the first time without a fuss.\""), .cross("Did {DL} explain why {D.he} was there?", "\"Yes. {D.He} said {D.he} was waiting to see a niece, and I told {D.him} that wasn't how pickup worked.\""), .cross("Could {DL} have gone to the front door and asked about the niece?", "\"Yes, and I would have explained the process. {D.He} chose not to come in.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} stood by a day care fence for twenty minutes after the director had warned {D.him} away.", "{DL} was waiting to see a niece who attends the day care and meant no harm to anyone."),
        allocution: "\"I was waiting by that fence, and I didn't think I was doing anything wrong, and I'd been warned. I've been in this courtroom before, and I know how that looks near children. I won't stand near that fence again.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} is not an approved pickup for any child at the day care, and {D.he} had been warned.", "{DL}'s niece does attend, and {D.he} stood outside the fence rather than going in because {D.he} is not on the pickup list."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why were you standing at the day care fence?", "\"I was waiting to see my niece, who goes to the day care. I hoped to see her on the playground and wave.\""), .direct("Had you been warned not to stand there?", "\"Yes, the director told me once. I didn't think I was doing anything wrong by waiting on the public sidewalk.\""), .direct("Why didn't you go to the front door?", "\"I'm not on the pickup list, and I didn't want to cause trouble. I thought waiting outside was the polite way to do it.\""), .direct("Did you speak to any child or touch the fence?", "\"No. I stood a few feet back on the sidewalk and watched. I never said a word to any child.\""), .direct("What did you do when the director called deputies?", "\"I stayed where I was and told the deputies about my niece. I gave them my name and my sister's phone number.\""), .direct("What will you do from now on?", "\"I won't stand near that fence again. If I want to see my niece, I'll ask my sister to arrange it.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I know how that looks near children. I understand why the director was worried about a stranger.\""), .cross("You were warned once already, weren't you?", "\"Yes, and I should have taken it more seriously. I'm sorry for the worry I caused the staff and parents.\""), .cross("You aren't on the approved pickup list, are you?", "\"No, I'm not. That's why I stood outside the fence and didn't try to go in.\""), .cross("You stood there for about twenty minutes, didn't you?", "\"About that long. I was hoping she'd come out to the playground, and I lost track of time.\""), .cross("You could have called your sister instead, couldn't you?", "\"I could have, and next time I will. It would have saved everyone a lot of trouble.\"")],
        openings: ("A day care director told {D} not to stand by the playground fence, and the day care camera shows {D} there again, watching the children for about twenty minutes. {D.He} is not an approved pickup, and {DL} came through this court in {PRIORDATE} where the matter was {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says {D.he} was waiting for a niece who attends, and was only hoping to see her. {D.He} never spoke to a child, never touched the gate and never meant to cause anyone worry, and the defense will show that."),
        closings: ("The director warned {D} once, and the camera shows {D} back at the fence, watching children, with no approved reason to be there. {DL} was in front of this court earlier, in {PRIORDATE} where the matter was {PRIOR}. Near a day care, a warning has to be obeyed.", "{DL}'s niece attends the day care, and {D} stood outside the fence hoping to see her. {D.He} never spoke to a child or tried to enter. A family member who waits outside is not a threat, and the State has shown nothing else."),
        timeline: [(-10, "The director sees {D} at the playground fence and warns {D.him} to stay away."), (0, "Afternoon: the day care camera shows {D} at the fence for about twenty minutes."), (0, "The director brings the children inside and calls deputies.")],
        identified: "Day Care Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let registerShove = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.registerShove",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Shopper Shoves Another at Self-Checkout"],
        law: "simpleAssault",
        spec: "Assaulted {V} by pushing {V.him}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} shoved a shopper at self-checkout.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Store Camera", "{D} pushes {V}.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Cut", "{DL} says {V} cut the line.")],
        role: "Attendant",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about your job at the store.", "\"I work as an attendant at the self-checkout area. I help customers with the machines, fix scanning problems and keep an eye on the lines.\""), .direct("What did you see at the register that day?", "\"I saw {D} shove a shopper who had stepped ahead in line. It happened quickly, with both hands to the chest.\""), .direct("What happened to the shopper after the shove?", "\"{V} stumbled sideways into a shopping cart and caught {V.his} balance on the handle. {V.He} looked shaken and held {V.his} arm.\""), .direct("What does the store camera show?", "\"It shows the line, {V} stepping ahead of {DL}, a short exchange of words, and then {DL} pushing {V.him} with both hands.\""), .direct("What did you do right after?", "\"I stepped between them and told them to stay apart. Then I called my manager, who called the sheriff's office.\""), .direct("Was {V} injured?", "\"{V.He} had a bruise on the upper arm by the next day. {V.He} told me it hurt, but {V.he} didn't need an ambulance.\""), .cross("Did {V} step ahead of {DL} in the line?", "\"From where I stood, it looked like {V.he} stepped in at the front, yes, though I couldn't hear what was said.\""), .cross("Did {V} say anything to {DL} before the shove?", "\"I believe {V.he} said something like asking to go first. I couldn't hear it clearly over the noise.\""), .cross("Did {DL} apologize afterward?", "\"Yes. {D.He} said sorry right away, and {D.he} looked upset with {D.himself}.\""), .cross("Did {DL} try to leave before the deputies arrived?", "\"No. {D.He} stayed at the register and waited, and {D.he} was calm when they came.\""), .cross("Was the store crowded?", "\"Fairly. There was a long line at the self-checkout, and people were getting impatient.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} shoved a shopper at a self-checkout station after a dispute over the line.", "{V} cut the line, and {DL} pushed {V.him} out of frustration and surprise."),
        allocution: "\"Someone cut in line at self-checkout, and I shoved them. I've been in this courtroom before for losing my temper. I should have just let it go or called a manager. I hope the shopper is all right.\"",
        truths: ("{V} had only a few items, and the store camera shows {D} shoving {V.him} with both hands.", "{V} had asked to go first, and {DL} reacted when {V.he} stepped ahead instead of waiting."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you shove {V} at the register?", "\"Yes, I did. {V.He} cut in line, and I shoved {V.him}, and I wish I hadn't.\""), .direct("What did {V} do before you pushed?", "\"{V.He} stepped right in front of me with a handful of items, as if the line wasn't there, and I'd been waiting for ten minutes.\""), .direct("Why did you push {V.him}?", "\"I lost my temper. I had a long day, and I was already late to pick up my kids. I didn't think before I used my hands.\""), .direct("What did you do after the shove?", "\"I said I was sorry right away. I stayed at the register and waited for a manager and the deputies.\""), .direct("Did you mean to hurt {V}?", "\"No. I just reacted, and I never meant to cause a bruise or any pain.\""), .direct("What would you do differently?", "\"I would have called a manager over or let it go. A few extra minutes in line was never worth this.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before for losing your temper, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I thought I'd learned something from it. I hadn't learned enough.\""), .cross("{V} was bruised because of your shove, wasn't {V.he}?", "\"Yes, and I'm truly sorry. I heard about the bruise, and I hope {V.he} is all right.\""), .cross("You could have walked away, couldn't you?", "\"I could have. I should have stepped back and let the attendant handle it.\""), .cross("You touched {V.him} first, didn't you?", "\"Yes. {V.He} never laid a hand on me. I'm the one who pushed.\""), .cross("You pushed with both hands, didn't you?", "\"I did. The camera shows it, and I won't say otherwise.\"")],
        openings: ("At a busy self-checkout, a shopper stepped ahead in the line, and the store camera shows {D} shoving {V.him} into a cart. {V.He} was left with a bruised arm, and {DL} was no stranger to this courtroom after {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says {V} cut the line, and {D.he} reacted before thinking. The defense will show a flash of anger over a few seconds in a crowded store, and {D.he} has said {D.he} is sorry."),
        closings: ("The store camera shows {D} shoving {V} into a cart over a place in line. {V} was bruised, and {DL} was in front of this court earlier, in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}. A person who pushes another over a line has committed an assault.", "{V} stepped ahead of {D} in a long line, and {D} reacted in a moment of frustration. {D.He} apologized at once and stayed for the deputies, and the State has not shown a plan to hurt anyone."),
        timeline: [(0, "{D} waits in a long line at the self-checkout."), (0, "{V} steps ahead, and {D} shoves {V.him} into a cart."), (0, "The attendant steps in and calls a manager, who calls deputies.")],
        identified: "Store Camera",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let barricadeTaken = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.barricadeTaken",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Road Barricades Taken From Work Zone"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole property of {V}, a contractor, valued at $420, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} loaded barricades from a work zone.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Work Zone Camera", "{D} loads barricades.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Discards", "{DL} says they looked discarded.")],
        role: "Site foreman",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about your job on the site.", "\"I'm the site foreman for a road contractor. I run the crew, keep track of our equipment and make sure the work zone is safe and properly marked.\""), .direct("What happened to your barricades?", "\"We'd closed the work zone and stacked the barricades by the road for the next shift. When we came back, a bunch were gone.\""), .direct("How many barricades were taken and what were they worth?", "\"About a dozen, and together they were worth around $420. They're heavy plastic with our company name stamped on the side.\""), .direct("What does the work zone camera show?", "\"It shows {D} backing a truck to the pile and loading barricades one at a time, in daylight, without any hurry.\""), .direct("Why can't barricades just be left lying around?", "\"We stage them for the next shift, and without them the traffic control plan fails. A missing barricade can leave a hazard unmarked.\""), .direct("What did you do after you saw the footage?", "\"I reported it to the sheriff's office with the video, and they traced the truck to {DL}.\""), .cross("Were the barricades stamped with your company name?", "\"Yes. The name is molded into each one and can be read from a few feet away.\""), .cross("Was the work zone closed at the time?", "\"The lane was closed, and work was done for the day. The barricades were stacked loosely at the edge.\""), .cross("Did {DL} try to hide while loading the barricades?", "\"No. {D.He} loaded them in plain view, with the camera on the pole above.\""), .cross("Did {DL} offer to return them?", "\"Yes. {D.He} told the deputy where they were and offered to bring them back.\""), .cross("Were all of the barricades recovered?", "\"Most of them were. A few are still missing.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} loaded barricades from a closed work zone into a truck and drove off with them.", "The barricades looked discarded and stacked as trash, and {DL} thought they were abandoned."),
        allocution: "\"I thought those barricades were trash from a closed work zone, and I loaded them up. I've been in this courtroom before, and I know I should have asked. I'll return every one or pay for them.\"",
        truths: ("The barricades were stamped with the contractor's name, which {DL} could see when loading them.", "They were stacked in a loose pile by the road, which looked like discarded equipment."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you load the barricades into your truck?", "\"Yes, I did. I thought they were trash from a closed work zone, and I loaded them up.\""), .direct("Why did you think they were discarded?", "\"They were stacked in a pile at the edge of the road, with no one around and the work zone closed. They looked left behind.\""), .direct("Did you see the contractor's name on them?", "\"I saw writing on them, but I didn't read it carefully. I wasn't thinking about whose they were.\""), .direct("Why did you load them in daylight?", "\"Because I thought it was fine. If I'd thought I was doing something wrong, I'd have waited for night.\""), .direct("What did you plan to do with them?", "\"I planned to use a few for my own property and to pass the rest on to friends. I know that's not an excuse.\""), .direct("What will you do about it now?", "\"I'll return every barricade I still have and pay for the ones that are gone.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I know I should have asked. I'm sorry for the trouble I caused.\""), .cross("You didn't ask anyone if you could take them, did you?", "\"No. I should have called the contractor or the town before I touched them.\""), .cross("The contractor's name is stamped on each barricade, isn't it?", "\"It is, and I know that now. I should have noticed it.\""), .cross("You took about a dozen, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I counted them as I loaded, and I'll return the ones I still have.\""), .cross("You were on camera the whole time, weren't you?", "\"Yes, and I'm not hiding it. I should have thought about the camera and about whose they were.\"")],
        openings: ("A contractor's barricades were stacked at the edge of a closed work zone, and the work zone camera shows {D} loading them into a truck. They were worth $420, and {DL} was last before this court in {PRIORDATE} in a case for {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says the barricades looked like trash from a work zone that was already closed, and {D.he} loaded them thinking they were discarded. The defense will show that {D.he} did so in the open and has offered to return every one."),
        closings: ("The work zone camera shows {D} loading stamped barricades into a truck in broad daylight. They carried the contractor's name and were worth $420. {DL} stood in this court once before, in {PRIORDATE} in a case for {PRIOR}.", "The barricades were stacked in a loose pile beside a closed work zone, and {D} believed they were abandoned. {D.He} loaded them openly and has offered to return or pay for every one. That is a mistake about ownership, not a plan to steal."),
        timeline: [(0, "Evening: the contractor stacks barricades beside the closed work zone."), (0, "Morning: the work zone camera shows {D} loading barricades into a truck."), (0, "The foreman finds the barricades missing and reports it.")],
        identified: "Work Zone Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let ebayEmpty = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.ebayEmpty",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Seller Ships Empty Box for Laptop"],
        law: "falsePretenses",
        spec: "Obtained property of {V} by deception, $1,200, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} took $1,200 for a laptop and shipped an empty box.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Shipping Box", "An empty box.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Mix-Up", "{DL} says boxes were swapped.")],
        role: "Buyer",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury how you came to buy a laptop from {D}.", "\"I found a listing for a laptop in good condition at $1,200. I'd been saving for one for school, and the seller had good reviews.\""), .direct("How did you pay?", "\"Through the site's payment system. The money left my account the same day, and the seller sent a tracking number.\""), .direct("What did you receive?", "\"A box that looked right on the outside, but it was empty. There was only some packing paper and a small piece of tape.\""), .direct("What did you do when you opened it?", "\"I took photos of the box and the packing, and I messaged the seller right away. Then I contacted the site.\""), .direct("How did {DL} respond?", "\"{D.He} said the boxes had been mixed up and that {D.he} would fix it. I haven't gotten a laptop or my money.\""), .direct("What has this cost you?", "\"$1,200 that I'd saved for months, plus the weeks I've spent trying to get it back. It's been very stressful.\""), .cross("Did the box weigh anything when it arrived?", "\"It felt light, but I didn't think about that until I opened it.\""), .cross("Did {DL} reply to your messages?", "\"Yes, a few times, and {D.he} was polite. {D.He} said it was a mistake.\""), .cross("Did {DL} offer a refund?", "\"{D.He} said {D.he} would, but the money hasn't come.\""), .cross("Do you know whether {DL} has other listings?", "\"I've seen a couple, and I don't know anything about them.\""), .cross("Was the tracking number real?", "\"Yes. It showed the box traveling to my address and being delivered.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} sold a laptop for $1,200 and shipped the buyer an empty box.", "{DL} mixed up two boxes at the shipping counter and never meant to send nothing."),
        allocution: "\"I may have mixed up the boxes when I shipped that laptop, and the buyer got an empty one. I've been in this courtroom before for something like this, and I'll refund the twelve hundred dollars right away.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had three other online listings for laptops, and the buyer received an empty box.", "The tracking shows only one box shipped, and {DL} had two similar boxes at home."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you ship {V} an empty box?", "\"Yes, I did, but I didn't mean to. I mixed up the boxes when I was shipping several packages.\""), .direct("How did the mix-up happen?", "\"I had two similar boxes at home, one with the laptop and one empty. I grabbed the wrong one at the shipping counter in a rush.\""), .direct("When did you find out?", "\"When {V} messaged me. I went home and found the laptop still sitting in the other box.\""), .direct("What did you do then?", "\"I told {V.him} it was a mistake and offered to ship the laptop or refund the money. {V.He} was understandably upset.\""), .direct("Why hasn't the money been refunded?", "\"I'd spent some of it paying bills, and I'm trying to gather what's left. I'll refund the whole $1,200.\""), .direct("What will you do from now on?", "\"I'll check every box before I seal it and photograph the contents. I should have done that.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before for something like this, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I understand how it looks. This time it was a real mix-up.\""), .cross("You have other laptops listed, don't you?", "\"I have a few listings, yes. I've never sent an empty box before.\""), .cross("The money has not been returned, has it?", "\"Not yet. I'm ashamed of that, and I'll fix it right away.\""), .cross("You still have the laptop, don't you?", "\"Yes. It's at my place, and I can send it right away.\""), .cross("The tracking shows only one box, doesn't it?", "\"It does. That's the empty one, and I'm sorry.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} paid $1,200 for a laptop through an online listing, and the box that arrived was empty. The shipping label shows {D} sent it. This is not {DL}'s first time here, since {PRIORDATE} brought {D.him} in once already in the case known as {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says the boxes were mixed up when {D.he} was shipping several packages at once, and {D.he} never meant to send an empty one. The defense will show that {D.he} has offered to refund the money in full."),
        closings: ("A buyer paid $1,200 for a laptop and received an empty box. The label, the receipt and the tracking all point to {D}. {DL} came through this court in {PRIORDATE} in a case for {PRIOR}. Taking money and shipping nothing is obtaining property by deception.", "The tracking shows one box and {D} had two similar ones at home. {DL} made a mistake at the shipping counter, and has offered to refund every dollar. The State has not shown {D.he} planned to send an empty box."),
        timeline: [(-10, "{D} lists a laptop online for $1,200."), (-5, "{V} pays and {D} ships a box."), (0, "{V} opens the box, finds it empty and reports it.")],
        identified: "Shipping Box",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let fittingRoomTwo = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.fittingRoomTwo",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Customer Wears Store Jacket Out of Fitting Room"],
        law: "larcenyMerchant",
        spec: "Took merchandise valued at $180 from {V}, a clothing store, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} wore a store jacket out of a fitting room.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Store Camera", "{D} walks out in a jacket.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Forgot", "{DL} says {D.he} forgot.")],
        role: "Store manager",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about your job at the store.", "\"I'm the store manager. I oversee the staff, handle loss prevention and review the camera when something goes missing.\""), .direct("What was reported?", "\"A jacket was missing from the fitting room rack, and the tag was found cut off in a stall. I reviewed the footage.\""), .direct("What does the camera show?", "\"{D} goes into the fitting room with the jacket, comes out wearing it under {D.his} own coat, and walks past the registers and out the door.\""), .direct("What was the jacket worth?", "\"$180 at full price. It was a new arrival, and we only had a few.\""), .direct("Did {DL} stop at a register?", "\"No. {D.He} walked directly past two registers and left through the front door.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I called the sheriff's office and gave them the footage. The next day, {DL} came back.\""), .cross("Did {DL} return to the store the same day?", "\"Yes, in the late afternoon. {D.He} came in and spoke to a clerk.\""), .cross("What did {DL} say when {D.he} came back?", "\"{D.He} said {D.he} had forgotten to pay and wanted to fix it.\""), .cross("Did {DL} try to hide the jacket under the coat?", "\"It was under the coat, but I can't say whether that was to hide it.\""), .cross("Did {DL} pay for the jacket?", "\"{D.He} offered to, but we had already called the deputies.\""), .cross("Did {DL} remove the tag?", "\"The tag was cut off in the fitting room. I can't say who did it.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} wore a store jacket out of a fitting room and past the registers without paying.", "{DL} put the jacket on to try it and walked out distracted, forgetting to pay."),
        allocution: "\"I put that jacket on in the fitting room and it was under my own coat, and I walked out distracted. I'll pay for the jacket today.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} removed the tag in the fitting room, and the camera shows {D.him} walking out in the jacket.", "{DL} came back to the store later the same day."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you walk out of the store in the jacket?", "\"Yes, I did. I put it on in the fitting room, and I walked out without paying.\""), .direct("Why did you put it on?", "\"I wanted to see how it fit, and I put my own coat over it. Then I got a call about my kids and left in a hurry.\""), .direct("Did you take off the tag?", "\"Yes. I cut it off in the stall so it wouldn't scratch my neck. I didn't think about what it would look like.\""), .direct("Why did you walk past the registers?", "\"I was distracted by my phone, and I forgot I was still wearing it. I didn't realize until I got to my car.\""), .direct("What did you do when you realized?", "\"I went back to the store that same day and told a clerk. I was embarrassed.\""), .direct("What will you do now?", "\"I'll pay for the jacket today, and I'm sorry for the trouble.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I know how that looks. I wasn't trying to steal.\""), .cross("You cut off the tag yourself, didn't you?", "\"I did, in the stall. I can see how that looks.\""), .cross("You walked past two registers, didn't you?", "\"I did, and I wasn't thinking.\""), .cross("You wore your own coat over it, didn't you?", "\"Yes, because it was cold outside, not to hide it.\""), .cross("You returned only after you were on camera, didn't you?", "\"I came back the same afternoon, before I knew anyone had called the deputies.\"")],
        openings: ("A clothing store camera shows {D} walk out of a fitting room wearing a $180 jacket under {D.his} own coat and leave through the front door. The tag was found in the fitting room, and {DL} was last before this court in {PRIORDATE} in the case known as {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says {D.he} put the jacket on to try it and walked out distracted, with no intent to leave without paying. The defense will show that {D.he} returned to the store the same day."),
        closings: ("The store camera shows {D} wearing a $180 jacket out the front door. The tag was cut off in the fitting room. The earlier case against {DL} was heard here in {PRIORDATE} where the matter was {PRIOR}. A jacket worn under a coat is a jacket taken.", "{D} walked out distracted and came back the same day. A person who returns to the store is not someone who meant to steal. {DL} will pay for the jacket today."),
        timeline: [(0, "{D} takes a jacket into a fitting room."), (0, "{D} removes the tag and walks out wearing the jacket under {D.his} coat."), (0, "Later that day: {D} returns to the store.")],
        identified: "Store Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .female])

    static let lotGateAgain = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.lotGateAgain",
        category: .traffic,
        headlines: ["Driver Plows Through Lot Gate Again"],
        law: "injuryPersonalProperty",
        spec: "Willfully and wantonly injured personal property of {V}, a parking operator, causing damage of $410, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} drove through another gate arm to avoid a fee.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Gate Camera", "{D} plows through.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Stuck", "{DL} says the gate stuck.")],
        role: "Garage manager",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about your job.", "\"I'm the manager of the parking garage. I oversee the staff, the gate equipment and the revenue, and I respond to damage.\""), .direct("What damage was reported?", "\"A gate arm at the exit lane was snapped in half, and pieces were lying across the lane. It's a gate that's raised and lowered by a motor.\""), .direct("What does the gate camera show?", "\"A car approaching the exit with no ticket, the arm rising for another car, and then the car driving through the arm as it came down.\""), .direct("What did the repair cost?", "\"The new arm, the motor repair and the labor came to $410, and the lane was closed for most of a day.\""), .direct("Did the driver stop?", "\"No. The car kept going after the arm snapped, but we got the plate from the camera.\""), .direct("How did you identify the driver?", "\"The plate was registered to {D}, and I called the sheriff's office with the footage.\""), .cross("Has that gate stuck before?", "\"Occasionally. We've had service calls on that lane, especially after rain.\""), .cross("Did {DL} have a ticket?", "\"No. I don't see one in the footage.\""), .cross("Did {DL} try to talk to an attendant?", "\"There was no attendant at that hour. There's an intercom, and I don't know whether {D.he} used it.\""), .cross("Did {DL} come back to apologize?", "\"{D.He} called later and offered to pay for the repair.\""), .cross("Did the gate come down on {DL}'s car?", "\"It looks that way on the footage. The arm was coming down as the car passed.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} drove through a parking garage gate arm to avoid a fee, breaking it.", "The gate was stuck, and {DL} drove through it because {D.he} couldn't pay the fee."),
        allocution: "\"The gate was stuck, and I drove through the arm to avoid a fee I couldn't pay. I've been in this courtroom before for the same thing. I'll cover the repair, and I'll find another way to pay.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had no ticket, and the gate raised for the car ahead and came down on {D.his}.", "The gate had stuck on the car ahead, and {DL} was caught under it."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you drive through the gate?", "\"Yes, I did. The gate was stuck, and I drove through it to avoid a fee I couldn't pay.\""), .direct("Why couldn't you pay the fee?", "\"I was out of cash, and my card had been declined at the garage that morning. I didn't have a ticket either.\""), .direct("What happened at the gate?", "\"It raised for the car ahead of me and started coming down on mine. I was afraid to stop, so I drove through.\""), .direct("Did you try the intercom?", "\"No. I was in a hurry and upset, and I didn't think about it.\""), .direct("What did you do afterward?", "\"I called the garage the next day and offered to pay for the repair.\""), .direct("What will you do now?", "\"I'll cover the repair, and I'll find another way to pay for parking.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before for the same thing, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I knew better. I'm ashamed of it.\""), .cross("You had no ticket, did you?", "\"No. I lost it, and I didn't want to pay the lost ticket fee.\""), .cross("You broke the arm, didn't you?", "\"Yes. It snapped as I drove through, and I'm sorry.\""), .cross("You drove away without telling anyone, didn't you?", "\"I did, and I called the next day.\""), .cross("You could have backed up, couldn't you?", "\"I could have, but there was a car behind me.\"")],
        openings: ("A parking operator's gate camera shows {D} driving through a gate arm without paying, and the arm snapped, causing $410 in damage. {DL} returns to this court having been here in {PRIORDATE} on the earlier matter, {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says the gate stuck and came down on the car, and that {D.he} drove through because {D.he} couldn't pay the fee. The defense will show a gate that had a history of sticking, and an act of desperation, not a plan to cause damage."),
        closings: ("The gate camera shows {D} driving through a gate arm, and it snapped. The damage was $410, and {DL} had no ticket. {DL} has appeared in this courtroom before, back in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}. Driving through a gate to avoid a fee is willful damage.", "The gate raised for the car ahead and came back down on {D}. {DL} was short on money and panicked. {D.He} has offered to pay for the repair and find another way to pay."),
        timeline: [(0, "{D} approaches the exit gate with no ticket."), (0, "The gate raises for the car ahead and comes down on {D}'s car."), (0, "{D} drives through the arm and it snaps.")],
        identified: "Gate Camera",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let wifiAgain = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.wifiAgain",
        category: .cyber,
        headlines: ["Man Uses Neighbor's Network After Password Change"],
        law: "accessingComputers",
        spec: "Accessed a computer network of {V} without authority, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} logged into a neighbor's network after a password change.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Router Log", "{D}'s laptop appears nightly.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Open", "{DL} says it was open.")],
        role: "Homeowner",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about your home network.", "\"I have a home wifi network that my family uses for work, school and streaming. I set it up myself, and I pay for it every month.\""), .direct("What made you check the router?", "\"The wifi had slowed down a lot in the evenings. I looked at the log and saw an unfamiliar laptop connecting every night.\""), .direct("What did you do about it?", "\"I changed the password, assuming that would end it. I also wrote down the name of the unknown device so I could track it.\""), .direct("What did you find afterward?", "\"The same laptop kept connecting at night, even after I had changed the password. It showed up in the router log every evening.\""), .direct("Who owns the laptop?", "\"The deputies traced the device name to {D}, who lives a couple of doors down the street from me.\""), .direct("Why do you consider this a problem?", "\"It's my network and I pay for it. I don't want people I haven't invited on it, whether they take anything or not.\""), .cross("Did {DL} open any of your files or devices?", "\"I have no sign that {D.he} did. The log shows only the connection times and the amount of traffic.\""), .cross("Is it possible the old password kept working after you changed it?", "\"I've since learned that the router didn't fully reset the old password, so it's possible, yes.\""), .cross("Did {DL} ever ask you for permission to use your wifi?", "\"No, {D.he} never did. We've never had more than a wave from the sidewalk.\""), .cross("Did the connections stop after the sheriff got involved?", "\"Yes, they stopped right away, and I haven't seen the laptop on the log since.\""), .cross("Had your network ever been open to anyone?", "\"Briefly, when I first set it up. I think {D.he} may have found it then.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} kept logging into a neighbor's wifi network every night after the password was changed.", "The network was open and the old password kept working, so {DL} believed {D.he} was still allowed to use it."),
        allocution: "\"The neighbor changed the password, and I got back in anyway. I've been in this courtroom before about this exact thing. I'll pay for my own internet from now on and stay off theirs.\"",
        truths: ("The password was changed and the router log still shows {DL}'s laptop connecting nightly afterward.", "The old password kept working because the router never fully reset, and {DL} saw no sign that anything had changed."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you log into your neighbor's network after the password changed?", "\"Yes, I did. The old password kept working, so I kept connecting at night.\""), .direct("Why did you connect to it in the first place?", "\"My own internet was cut off for non-payment, and I needed it to look for jobs and talk to my kids.\""), .direct("Did you know the password had been changed?", "\"I didn't know for certain. My old password still worked, so I figured it was fine and kept using it.\""), .direct("What did you do on the network?", "\"I looked for jobs, checked my email and watched a few videos. I never went near anyone's files or devices.\""), .direct("What did you do when the deputies came to see you?", "\"I told them everything, handed over my laptop and stopped connecting that same night.\""), .direct("What will you do from now on?", "\"I'll pay for my own internet and stay off my neighbor's network. I should have asked for permission in the first place.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before about this exact thing, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I should have known better. I'm embarrassed to be standing here a second time over wifi.\""), .cross("You never asked your neighbor for permission, did you?", "\"No, I never did. I was too embarrassed to ask, and that was my mistake.\""), .cross("You connected almost every night, didn't you?", "\"Most nights, yes. It became a habit, and I stopped thinking about whose network it was.\""), .cross("The password had been changed, hadn't it?", "\"Apparently so, but my old one kept working. I should have realized that something was off.\""), .cross("You used a network you weren't paying for, didn't you?", "\"Yes, and I'm sorry. I understand why my neighbor was upset.\"")],
        openings: ("A homeowner changed the wifi password after noticing slow service, and the router log still shows {D}'s laptop connecting every night. {DL} was no stranger to this courtroom after {PRIORDATE} when the case concerned {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says the network was open and the old password kept working, so {D.he} thought it was fine. The defense will show that {D.he} never tried to open any files or devices and has offered to pay for {D.his} own internet."),
        closings: ("The router log shows {D}'s laptop connecting night after night after the password was changed. This is not {DL}'s first time here, since {PRIORDATE} brought {D.him} in once already after being charged with {PRIOR}. A changed password is a closed door, and {DL} kept going through it.", "The old password kept working, and {D} never looked at a file. {DL} believed {D.he} was allowed, and has promised to pay for {D.his} own internet from now on."),
        timeline: [(-14, "The homeowner notices slow wifi and changes the password."), (0, "The router log shows {D}'s laptop connecting every night after the change."), (0, "The homeowner reports the connections to deputies.")],
        identified: "Router Log",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let curbBed = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.curbBed",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Man Takes Mattress From Curb That Was Not Free"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole property of {V}, valued at $350, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} loaded a mattress from a curb that its owner was selling.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Doorbell Camera", "{D} loads the mattress.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Free", "{DL} says curb items are free.")],
        role: "Owner",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about the mattress.", "\"It was a nearly new queen mattress that I was selling for $350. I put it at the curb with a sign so people walking by could see it.\""), .direct("What did the sign say?", "\"It said 'For sale, $350, call this number.' I taped it to the side of the mattress facing the street so nobody could miss it.\""), .direct("What happened that day?", "\"I came home from work and the mattress was gone. I checked my doorbell camera to see who had taken it.\""), .direct("What does the camera show?", "\"It shows {D} pulling up in a truck, looking around, and loading the mattress. {D.He} didn't stop to look at the sign or knock.\""), .direct("Did {DL} contact you afterward?", "\"No, I never heard from {D.him} until the deputies told me who it was. By then the mattress was already in {D.his} house.\""), .direct("What did this cost you?", "\"I lost the $350 I would have been paid for it, and I spent an evening dealing with the sheriff's office.\""), .cross("Was the sign facing the street when you left?", "\"I believe so, but it was held on with tape and could have slipped. It might have fallen face down.\""), .cross("Do people often take things left at a curb in your neighborhood?", "\"Yes, it happens all the time here. Some of my neighbors put out furniture to be taken.\""), .cross("Did {DL} seem to be sneaking when {D.he} loaded the mattress?", "\"No. {D.He} did it in daylight, in plain view, and it didn't look secretive at all.\""), .cross("Did {DL} offer to return it?", "\"Through the deputies, yes. {D.He} said {D.he} would bring it back or pay for it.\""), .cross("Have you put signs on items at the curb before?", "\"Occasionally, but this was the first time one was taken.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} loaded a mattress off a curb that its owner had put out for sale.", "{DL} believed anything left at a curb was free, and never saw a for-sale sign."),
        allocution: "\"That mattress was at the curb, and I thought it was free. The owner was selling it, and I didn't see a sign. I've been in this courtroom before about a couch. I'll pay for it or bring it back.\"",
        truths: ("A for-sale sign was taped to the mattress and the doorbell camera shows {D} loading it.", "The sign had fallen face down, so nothing on the street side told {DL} it was for sale."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take the mattress from the curb?", "\"Yes, I did. It was at the curb, and I thought it was free for the taking.\""), .direct("Did you see a for-sale sign?", "\"No. If there was one, it was face down or on the side I couldn't see from the truck.\""), .direct("Why did you think it was free?", "\"In this neighborhood, anything left at the curb is usually meant to be thrown out. I've picked up furniture the same way before.\""), .direct("Why did you load it in broad daylight?", "\"Because I thought it was fine. If I'd known it was for sale, I never would have done it in front of a camera.\""), .direct("What did you plan to do with it?", "\"I planned to put it in my spare room for my niece, who was coming to stay. I didn't plan to resell it.\""), .direct("What will you do now?", "\"I'll either bring the mattress back or pay the owner the $350. I should have knocked on the door first.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before about a couch, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I thought I'd learned my lesson. I should have checked more carefully this time.\""), .cross("You didn't look for a sign before loading it, did you?", "\"No, I didn't, and I should have. I was in a hurry.\""), .cross("The mattress looked nearly new, didn't it?", "\"It did, and that should have made me wonder why anyone would throw it away.\""), .cross("You didn't knock on the door to ask, did you?", "\"No. I should have, and I'm sorry that I didn't.\""), .cross("You took it without asking permission, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I did, and I understand why the owner is upset about it.\"")],
        openings: ("A homeowner put a nearly new mattress at the curb with a for-sale sign, and the doorbell camera shows {D} loading it into a truck. The mattress was worth $350. {DL} already has a history in this court, dating to {PRIORDATE} in the case known as {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says anything left at a curb is free, and the sign was face down where {D.he} saw it. The defense will show that {D.he} loaded it in daylight and has offered to bring it back or pay the owner."),
        closings: ("The doorbell camera shows {D} loading a mattress that had a for-sale sign on it. {DL} stood in this court once before, in {PRIORDATE} on the earlier matter, {PRIOR}. A sign means the item is not free, and the owner wanted $350.", "The sign was face down, and {D} saw a mattress at a curb. {DL} thought it was free, loaded it in daylight, and has offered to return it or pay the price."),
        timeline: [(0, "Morning: the owner sets the mattress at the curb with a for-sale sign."), (0, "Midday: the doorbell camera shows {D} backing a truck up and loading the mattress."), (0, "Evening: the owner comes home, finds the mattress gone and reports it.")],
        identified: "Doorbell Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let barrelAgain = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.barrelAgain",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Man Keeps Burning Trash After Fire Marshal Visit"],
