        spec: "Disturbed the peace of {V}, a neighbor, by burning refuse, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} burned trash again after a fire marshal warning.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Neighbor Camera", "Smoke from {D}'s yard.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Permit", "{DL} says {D.he} burns yard waste.")],
        role: "Neighbor",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury where you live in relation to {D}.", "\"I live next door to {DL}. Our back yards share a fence, and the smoke from {D.his} barrel blows straight over my deck and into my open windows.\""), .direct("What did you see that afternoon?", "\"A thick gray plume of smoke came over the fence. I could smell burning plastic, and it made my eyes water and my kids cough.\""), .direct("What does your camera show?", "\"It shows the barrel in {DL}'s yard with smoke pouring out of it for over an hour, and {DL} tossing things in from time to time.\""), .direct("Had the fire marshal spoken to {DL} before?", "\"Yes, a few weeks earlier. The marshal told {DL} to stop burning trash, and I thought that would be the end of it.\""), .direct("What did you do when it happened again?", "\"I called the fire marshal's office, and the marshal came out and looked in the barrel. There was melted plastic in with the ashes.\""), .direct("How did the smoke affect your family?", "\"We had to close all the windows, and my daughter, who has asthma, needed her inhaler. We couldn't use the yard that afternoon.\""), .cross("Did you see {DL} put plastic in the barrel?", "\"No. I saw {D.him} tossing things in, but I couldn't tell what they were from that distance.\""), .cross("Do many people in your neighborhood burn leaves and brush?", "\"Some do, yes, especially in the fall. It's allowed in this county with a permit for certain materials.\""), .cross("Have you and {DL} had disagreements before?", "\"A few over the fence line and a dog. Nothing serious, but we aren't friendly.\""), .cross("Did {DL} put out the fire when the marshal arrived?", "\"Yes. {D.He} put it out right away and was polite about it.\""), .cross("Has the smoke come from {DL}'s yard since that day?", "\"No, not since the marshal's visit.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} burned trash in a barrel again after a fire marshal's warning, sending smoke over the neighbors.", "{DL} was burning only yard waste, which {D.he} believed was allowed."),
        allocution: "\"I burned leaves again after the fire marshal told me not to. I've been in this courtroom before, and I know it's a nuisance to my neighbors. I'll haul my yard waste to the county site from now on.\"",
        truths: ("A fire marshal had already warned {DL}, and plastic was in the barrel along with the leaves.", "{DL} only meant to burn leaves and branches, and the plastic came from a bag that fell in."),
        defendant: [.direct("Were you burning trash in the barrel?", "\"I was burning leaves and branches. A bag with some plastic fell in by accident, and I didn't notice it right away.\""), .direct("Did you know the fire marshal had warned you?", "\"Yes, I did. I understood the warning to be about burning household trash, and I thought yard waste was different.\""), .direct("Did you have a permit?", "\"I thought I didn't need one for leaves. I've since learned the rules, and I'll get what I need if I burn again.\""), .direct("Why did you burn instead of hauling the waste away?", "\"I don't have a truck, and the county site is far from my house. Burning was the easiest way.\""), .direct("What did you do when the marshal came?", "\"I put the fire out right away, and I answered all of his questions. I told him about the bag.\""), .direct("What will you do from now on?", "\"I'll haul my yard waste to the county site, and I'll make sure nothing but leaves goes into a fire.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I know it's a nuisance to my neighbors. I'm sorry for the smoke.\""), .cross("The marshal warned you once already, didn't he?", "\"Yes, and I should have taken the warning more seriously.\""), .cross("There was plastic in the barrel, wasn't there?", "\"Yes, and I take responsibility for that. I should have checked before I lit it.\""), .cross("Your neighbor has a child with asthma, doesn't she?", "\"I didn't know that until now, and I'm very sorry.\""), .cross("You kept burning after you saw the smoke going over the fence, didn't you?", "\"I did, for a while. I should have put it out sooner.\"")],
        openings: ("A neighbor's camera shows heavy smoke rising from {D}'s yard, and a fire marshal had already warned {D.him} once about burning trash. Plastic was found in the barrel afterward, and {DL} has appeared in this courtroom before, back in {PRIORDATE} after being charged with {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says {D.he} was burning yard waste, which {D.he} believed was allowed, and the plastic ended up in the barrel by accident. The defense will show a neighbor dispute over smoke and a property owner who did not mean to cause a nuisance."),
        closings: ("A fire marshal warned {D} not to burn trash in a barrel, and the neighbor's camera shows smoke rising from {D}'s yard again. Plastic was in the barrel. {DL} was in front of this court earlier, in {PRIORDATE} on the earlier matter, {PRIOR}. A warning that is ignored becomes a nuisance.", "{D} was burning leaves and branches, as many people in the county do. The plastic fell in by accident. {DL} did not mean to bother anyone and will haul yard waste to the county site from now on."),
        timeline: [(-20, "A fire marshal warns {D} not to burn trash in the barrel."), (0, "Afternoon: the neighbor's camera shows heavy smoke from {D}'s yard."), (0, "The neighbor calls the fire marshal, who finds plastic in the barrel.")],
        identified: "Neighbor Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let paradeAgain = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.paradeAgain",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Man Blocks Holiday Parade Float"],
        law: "disorderly",
        spec: "Disturbed the peace by blocking a public event, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: false,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} stood in front of a holiday parade float.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Street Camera", "{D} blocks a float.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Protest", "{DL} says it was a protest.")],
        role: "Parade marshal",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about your role at the parade.", "\"I'm a parade marshal. I volunteer each year to keep the floats moving in order and to keep the route clear for the families and groups watching.\""), .direct("What happened that morning?", "\"About forty minutes into the parade, {D} walked out of the crowd and stood directly in front of one of the floats. The float had to stop.\""), .direct("What was {DL} doing?", "\"{DL} was holding a sign, standing still and looking straight ahead. {D.He} didn't speak to me or to anyone on the float.\""), .direct("How long was the float stopped?", "\"About ten minutes. The floats behind it had to stop too, and the whole parade backed up along the route.\""), .direct("Were there people close by?", "\"Yes, families with small children lined the curb a few feet away. The float had children on it too.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I asked {DL} to move, and when {D.he} didn't, I called the deputies. They walked {D.him} off the street.\""), .cross("Did {DL} touch the float or anyone on it?", "\"No. {D.He} just stood there. I never saw {D.him} reach out or try to climb on anything.\""), .cross("Did {DL} threaten anyone?", "\"No, not that I heard. {D.He} was quiet.\""), .cross("Did {DL} have a permit to protest?", "\"Not that I know of. Parades require permits, and I haven't seen one.\""), .cross("Did {DL} resist when the deputies came?", "\"No. {D.He} went with them without a struggle.\""), .cross("Was anyone hurt?", "\"No, nobody was hurt, but it could have gone wrong with a float and a crowd that close.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} stood in front of a holiday parade float and blocked it.", "It was a protest, and {DL} meant to make a point, not to endanger anyone."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry for standing in front of that float. I did it to protest, and I've been in this courtroom before for the same cause. I care about it, but I understand I put families at risk. I'll find a safer way to make my point.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had a sign and no permit, and the camera shows {D.him} blocking the float.", "{DL} has protested the same cause before, and stood still in front of the float rather than rush it."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you stand in front of the parade float?", "\"Yes, I did. I wanted to make a point about something I care about, and I stood in front of it with a sign.\""), .direct("What was your sign about?", "\"It was about the cause I've been protesting for years. I won't go into all of it, but it's something I take very seriously.\""), .direct("Did you touch the float or any person?", "\"No. I stood still the whole time. I never reached for anything or spoke loudly.\""), .direct("Why did you choose a parade?", "\"That's where the crowds are. I wanted people to see the sign, and I didn't think about how it would affect the families.\""), .direct("What did you do when the deputies came?", "\"I walked with them without a fight. I told them I'd been protesting peacefully.\""), .direct("What would you do differently?", "\"I'd find a safer way to make my point, like standing on the sidewalk with the sign or getting a permit.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before for the same cause, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I care about it deeply. I should have done it a different way.\""), .cross("You didn't have a permit, did you?", "\"No, I did not. I should have asked, and I'm sorry.\""), .cross("You stopped the whole parade, didn't you?", "\"I did, and I regret the families who missed their time.\""), .cross("There were children on that float, weren't there?", "\"Yes, I saw them. I didn't mean to scare them.\""), .cross("You could have stood on the curb with your sign, couldn't you?", "\"I could have. I chose not to.\"")],
        openings: ("At a holiday parade, the street camera shows {D} stepping in front of a moving float and blocking it for several minutes. Families were close by, and The earlier case against {DL} was heard here in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says it was a protest. {D.He} stood still and held a sign, and the defense will show that {D.he} did not touch the float, did not touch anyone and had no plan to hurt a soul."),
        closings: ("The street camera shows {D} stepping in front of a parade float and holding it up while families watched from the curb. The court file shows {DL} here in {PRIORDATE} where the matter was {PRIOR}. Parades have rules, and so do protests.", "{D} stood still with a sign, and touched nobody. {DL} cares about the cause, and has said that {D.he} will find a safer way to make the point. A quiet protest is not a disturbance of the peace."),
        timeline: [(0, "10 a.m.: the holiday parade begins on the main street."), (0, "10:40 a.m.: {D} steps in front of a float with a sign and stops it."), (0, "10:50 a.m.: deputies remove {D} from the street and the parade resumes.")],
        identified: "Street Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let receptionCrash = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.receptionCrash",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Man Crashes Retirement Party and Refuses to Leave"],
