        role: "Deputy",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about your job.", "\"I'm a deputy with the sheriff's office. I patrol the roads, enforce traffic laws and check registrations and tags during stops.\""), .direct("Why did you stop {D}'s car?", "\"The temporary tag looked odd, with the print fuzzy and the font wrong. I ran the number, and it didn't come back to any record.\""), .direct("What did you do next?", "\"I pulled {DL} over, asked for the registration and compared the tag to a genuine one from my training materials.\""), .direct("What did you find about the tag?", "\"It was printed on regular paper, laminated, and the number was invalid. The state seal looked copied from another document.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say about it?", "\"{D.He} said the tag was a prop, because the car was for sale, and {D.he} hadn't meant it as real registration.\""), .direct("What happened to the car?", "\"It was parked at a lot while we sorted out ownership. {DL}'s name was on the title.\""), .cross("Was the car listed for sale?", "\"I saw a listing on {D.his} phone, and a buyer was texting {D.him} at the stop.\""), .cross("Did {DL} try to hide the tag?", "\"No. It was on the car in plain sight.\""), .cross("Did {DL} have a valid registration?", "\"The car had expired, as far as I could tell. {D.He} said {D.he} was in the process of selling.\""), .cross("Did {DL} cooperate?", "\"Yes. {D.He} handed over the tag and answered my questions.\""), .cross("How common are fake tags in your experience?", "\"It's fairly common, but most are made to avoid fees, not as props.\"")],
