        truths: ("The tag had a bad number and was printed on a home printer, and {DL} drove with it on the car.", "The car was listed for sale, and a buyer was texting {DL} about the car."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you make the tag?", "\"Yes, I did, and I thought of it as a prop. The car was for sale, and I wanted it to look presentable.\""), .direct("Why did you put it on the car?", "\"A buyer was coming to see the car, and I thought the tag would make it look ready to go. I didn't think about the law.\""), .direct("Did you drive with the tag on?", "\"Yes, to pick up a part. I should have taken it off, and I'm sorry I didn't.\""), .direct("What did you tell the deputy?", "\"That the tag was fake, and why I made it. I handed it over right away.\""), .direct("Did you mean to deceive anyone?", "\"No. I didn't think it could be mistaken for real, and I never tried to pass it off.\""), .direct("What will you do about it?", "\"I'll register the car properly, and I won't make anything like that again.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I know that isn't an excuse. I should have done it right.\""), .cross("The tag had a bad number, didn't it?", "\"Yes, I made up a number. I didn't think it would be checked.\""), .cross("You drove on a public road with it, didn't you?", "\"I did, for a short trip.\""), .cross("The car's registration had expired, hadn't it?", "\"Yes. I was selling it, and I let it lapse.\""), .cross("You copied the state seal, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I printed it from an image.\"")],
        openings: ("A deputy stopped a car with a temporary tag that did not match any record, and the tag turned out to be printed at home. The number was invalid, and The earlier case against {DL} was heard here in {PRIORDATE} where the matter was {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says the tag was a prop for a car that was listed for sale, and that {D.he} never meant it to look real. The defense will show a buyer texting about the car and an owner who was trying to sell, not to deceive anyone."),
        closings: ("The deputy found a tag with a bad number, printed at home, on a car {D} was driving. The court file shows {DL} here in {PRIORDATE} in a case for {PRIOR}. A fake tag is a forged state record.", "{D} put the tag on a car that was for sale, and did not mean it to pass. A buyer was texting about the car that day. {DL} will register the car properly."),
        timeline: [(0, "{D} prints a temporary tag at home and puts it on the car."), (0, "A deputy runs the plate and finds that the number does not exist."), (0, "The deputy stops {D}, seizes the tag and calls a supervisor.")],
