        defendant: [.direct("Did you put the sticker on your plate?", "\"Yes, I did, but I bought it from a shop that told me it was real, and I believed that when I put it on.\""), .direct("Where did you buy it?", "\"From a small shop that handled tags and registrations. A friend told me about it, and I paid cash and got a printed receipt.\""), .direct("Why didn't you go to the DMV yourself?", "\"I'd heard the line was very long, and I was short on time that week. I thought the shop was a shortcut.\""), .direct("Did you know the sticker was fake?", "\"No, I didn't. I would never have put it on my car if I'd known it was a copy.\""), .direct("What did you do when the trooper stopped you?", "\"I told {TROOPER.him} exactly where I'd bought it and showed {TROOPER.him} the receipt. I handed over the sticker without arguing.\""), .direct("What will you do now?", "\"I'll register the car properly with the DMV and pay whatever fine the court sets. I'm sorry for the trouble.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I know I should have gone to the DMV myself. I took a shortcut and it caught up with me.\""), .cross("The shop you describe doesn't exist, does it?", "\"That's what I've been told, and I was fooled by it. I'd like to help find whoever was behind it.\""), .cross("You paid in cash, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I did. That's all they took, and I didn't think anything of it at the time.\""), .cross("Your real registration had expired, hadn't it?", "\"Yes, it had. I let it lapse, and I should have renewed it on time.\""), .cross("You put the sticker on the plate yourself, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I peeled it off the backing and stuck it on in my driveway, as the shop told me.\"")],
        openings: ("A state trooper stopped a car with a registration sticker that was a copy, and the car belongs to {D}. The shop that supposedly sold it does not exist, and {DL} came through this court in {PRIORDATE} after being charged with {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says {D.he} bought the sticker from a shop and believed it was real. The defense will show a receipt, and an owner who was taken in by a seller and did not make anything."),
        closings: ("The sticker on {D}'s plate was a copy, and the shop that supposedly sold it does not exist. This is not {DL}'s first time here, since {PRIORDATE} brought {D.him} in once already for {PRIOR}. A forged registration is a crime against the state.", "{DL} has a receipt and believed the sticker was real. {D.He} did not make it and will register the car properly and pay any fine the court sets."),
        timeline: [(-10, "{D} buys a registration sticker from a shop and puts it on the plate."), (0, "A trooper notices the sticker looks off and runs the plate."), (0, "The trooper stops {D} and finds that the sticker is a copy.")],
