        headlines: ["Dog Owners Fight at Second Park"],
        law: "simpleAssault",
        spec: "Assaulted {V} by striking {V.him}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} punched another dog owner after a leash dispute.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Park Camera", "{D} punches {V}.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Leash", "{DL} says the dog lunged.")],
        role: "Park attendant",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about your job at the park.", "\"I'm an attendant at the park. I check that dogs are vaccinated, remind owners of the leash rules and break up fights.\""), .direct("What did you see that day?", "\"I saw two owners arguing over a leash near the gate. Their dogs were circling each other, and the voices were getting louder.\""), .direct("What happened next?", "\"The dogs got tangled, and {D} swung at {V}. {V} was hit in the face and staggered back.\""), .direct("What injuries did {V} have?", "\"A bloody nose and a swollen cheek. {V.He} sat on a bench holding a towel until deputies came.\""), .direct("What did the park camera show?", "\"{DL} stepping forward and punching {V} once, with the dogs close to both of them.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I stepped between them, took the dogs by the leashes and called the sheriff's office.\""), .cross("Was {V}'s dog on a leash?", "\"It wasn't, at least not when I first noticed. I think {V.he} had just taken it off.\""), .cross("Did {V} say anything to {DL} first?", "\"They were arguing. I think {V.he} said sorry, but I couldn't hear clearly.\""), .cross("Did {DL}'s dog lunge at {V}?", "\"It moved toward {V}, yes. I can't say it was an attack.\""), .cross("Did {DL} stay after the punch?", "\"Yes. {D.He} stayed and asked if {V} was all right.\""), .cross("Had you seen {DL} fight before?", "\"No, never at this park.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} punched another dog owner in a park after a dispute over a leash.", "{D.His} dog lunged at {V}, and {DL} struck out while trying to protect it."),
        allocution: "\"Our dogs got tangled over the leash, and I punched the other owner. I've been in this courtroom before for the same thing, and I should have just walked my dog away. I hope the owner is okay.\"",
        truths: ("{V} had let the dog off leash, and {V.he} said sorry first before the punch.", "The other dog lunged, and {DL} reacted in the confusion."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you punch {V}?", "\"Yes, I did. Our dogs got tangled over the leash, and {V.he} came at me, and I punched {V.him}. I reacted without thinking.\""), .direct("How did the argument start?", "\"{V}'s dog was off leash and ran at mine. We argued about it, and then the dogs tangled and started pulling.\""), .direct("What did you feel when the dogs tangled?", "\"I was afraid for my dog and for myself. I thought {V.he} was about to hit me, and I struck first.\""), .direct("What did you do after you punched {V}?", "\"I stepped back and asked if {V.he} was okay. I felt awful, and I stayed until the attendant came.\""), .direct("Did you mean to hurt {V}?", "\"I meant to stop what I thought was coming. I never meant for {V.him} to get hurt.\""), .direct("What would you do differently?", "\"I'd walk my dog away, and let the attendant handle it. I shouldn't have swung at anyone.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before for the same thing, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I should have just walked my dog away. I'm sorry and ashamed.\""), .cross("{V} had a bloody nose, didn't {V.he}?", "\"Yes, and I'm sorry about that. I hope {V.he} is all right.\""), .cross("You struck first, didn't you?", "\"Yes, in the sense that I hit {V.him}. I thought I was defending myself.\""), .cross("You could have walked away, couldn't you?", "\"I could have done that, and I know now that I should have.\""), .cross("The dogs weren't fighting when you punched, were they?", "\"They were tangled and pulling. It looked bad to me.\"")],
        openings: ("At a dog park, a camera shows {D} punch {V}, another dog owner, after an argument over a leash. {V} was struck in the face, and {DL} returns to this court having been here in {PRIORDATE} after being charged with {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says the dogs got tangled over the leash, and {D.he} reacted in the confusion. The defense will show a split-second mistake in a crowded park, and an owner who regrets it and checked on {V.him} afterward."),
        closings: ("The park camera shows {D} punching {V} in the face after a leash dispute. {V} had done nothing but argue. {DL} came through this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}.", "The dogs tangled over the leash, and {D} struck out in the confusion. {D.He} is sorry and has asked about {V}. A mistake in a crowded park is not the same as a planned attack."),
        timeline: [(0, "{D} and {V} argue over a leash at the dog park."), (0, "The dogs tangle, and {D} punches {V}."), (0, "The park attendant separates them and calls deputies.")],
        identified: "Park Camera",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let barberDeposit = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.barberDeposit",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Barber Takes Chair-Rental Deposits Then Vanishes"],
        law: "falsePretenses",
        spec: "Obtained property of {V} by deception, $600, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} took chair-rental deposits totaling $600 and vanished.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Receipts", "Three deposits to {D}.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Closure", "{DL} says the building was sold.")],
        role: "Renter",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury how you came to meet {D}.", "\"I'm a barber. {DL} was opening a new shop and asked barbers to rent a chair, with a deposit to hold it.\""), .direct("How much did you pay?", "\"$200 for my chair deposit, in cash. {DL} wrote me a receipt, and two other barbers paid the same.\""), .direct("What did {DL} promise you?", "\"That the shop would open at the start of the next month, with my own station and a lease for the chair.\""), .direct("What happened on opening day?", "\"The door was locked, and a sign said the building had been sold. There was nobody to talk to.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I called {DL}, and the calls went to voicemail. I left messages for days, and then I went to the sheriff's office.\""), .direct("What did the loss mean to you?", "\"$200 is a lot for me. I'd turned down another shop to take that chair, and I was out of work for weeks.\""), .cross("Did {DL} give you a receipt?", "\"Yes. It was handwritten, with the date and the amount.\""), .cross("Did {DL} say anything about the building being sold?", "\"No, not before the deposit. I heard about it later.\""), .cross("Did {DL} ever call you back?", "\"Eventually, yes. {D.He} said the sale was a surprise and promised to refund.\""), .cross("Have you been repaid?", "\"Not yet. {D.He} has offered, but I haven't received anything.\""), .cross("Did you see the building for sale yourself?", "\"I saw a sign later, after the shop was locked.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took $600 in chair-rental deposits from three barbers and then closed the shop.", "The building was sold, and {DL} meant to reopen the shop elsewhere and refund the deposits."),
        allocution: "\"I hoped to reopen that shop, and I took those chair-rental deposits meaning to. I've been in this courtroom before, and I should have called every renter. I'll repay the six hundred dollars.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} kept taking deposits after knowing the building was for sale, and the receipts show three payments.", "The building sale closed only after the deposits were taken, and {DL} hoped to reopen."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take chair-rental deposits from three barbers?", "\"Yes, I did. I took $600 in total from three barbers, and at the time I fully meant to open the shop.\""), .direct("Why didn't the shop open?", "\"The building was sold, and the new owner wanted the space for something else. I'd been hoping to find another place and reopen quickly.\""), .direct("Did you know about the sale when you took the deposits?", "\"I knew the building was on the market, but I hadn't been told it was actually selling. I thought I had more time than I did.\""), .direct("Why didn't you call the barbers right away?", "\"I was embarrassed, and I was searching for a new space. I kept thinking I could fix it myself before anyone had to know.\""), .direct("What did you do with the money?", "\"I put some of it into the shop's own deposit and some into overdue bills. Part of it is gone, and I'll have to make it up.\""), .direct("What will you do now?", "\"I'll repay every barber the full $600, and I'll apologize to each of them face to face for the trouble I caused.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I should have called every renter the moment the sale came up. I let them down.\""), .cross("You took the money before the building was secure, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I did, and I can see now that it was a mistake. I should have waited until the lease was signed.\""), .cross("You didn't tell the barbers the building was for sale, did you?", "\"No, I didn't tell them. I was afraid they would back out, and I kept it to myself.\""), .cross("You have not repaid them yet, have you?", "\"Not yet, and I'm ashamed of that. I'm gathering the money, and I'll pay as soon as I can.\""), .cross("The barbers lost work because of what happened, didn't they?", "\"Some of them did, and I'm sorry. I know a missed month is hard for anyone who cuts hair for a living.\"")],
        openings: ("Three barbers each paid {D} a chair-rental deposit for a new shop, totaling $600, and then the shop never opened. Receipts show the payments went to {D}, and The earlier case against {DL} was heard here in {PRIORDATE} where the matter was {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says the building was sold out from under the shop, and {D.he} hoped to reopen it elsewhere. The defense will show a business that failed, not a plan to take deposits and vanish."),
        closings: ("Three barbers paid deposits totaling $600, and the shop never opened. The receipts show every payment went to {D}, who kept taking deposits after the building went on the market. The court file shows {DL} here in {PRIORDATE} in a case for {PRIOR}.", "The building was sold, and {D} hoped to reopen elsewhere. A business failure is not a fraud. {DL} has promised to repay every barber the $600."),
        timeline: [(-30, "{D} begins taking chair-rental deposits for a new barber shop."), (-10, "The building goes on the market and a sale is arranged."), (0, "The sale closes, the shop never opens and the barbers cannot reach {D}.")],
        identified: "Receipts",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let duckCoop = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.duckCoop",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Man Takes Ducks From Pond Pen"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole property of {V}, valued at $200, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} took eight ducks from a pond pen.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Yard Camera", "{D} carries a crate.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Stray", "{DL} says the ducks were loose.")],
        role: "Homeowner",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about your ducks.", "\"We keep eight ducks in a pen beside the pond in our back yard. They've been with our family for two years, and the children named every one.\""), .direct("What happened that day?", "\"I fed them and latched the pen in the morning. When I came back in the afternoon, the pen was open and the ducks were gone.\""), .direct("What does your yard camera show?", "\"It shows {D} walking up to the pond with a crate, opening the pen and putting the ducks into the crate one at a time.\""), .direct("How did you know the pen had been latched?", "\"I latch it every day. It has a hook-and-eye latch that a duck can't open, and it was open when I got back.\""), .direct("What were the ducks worth?", "\"About $200, between the cost of the birds and the supplies. To my family, they were worth far more.\""), .direct("What happened after you called the sheriff?", "\"Deputies found the ducks at {DL}'s home a few days later. All eight were alive and well, and they came back to us.\""), .cross("Did {DL} hurt the ducks?", "\"No. They were in a clean pen and well fed.\""), .cross("Could the ducks sometimes wander from the pen?", "\"Occasionally, when the latch was left loose, but never far.\""), .cross("Did {DL} say why {D.he} took them?", "\"{D.He} said {D.he} thought they were strays at the pond.\""), .cross("Did {DL} offer to pay for anything?", "\"Yes, {D.he} offered to pay for the ducks and for the cost of the pen repair.\""), .cross("Did you ever speak to {DL} before this?", "\"No, I'd never met {D.him}.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took eight ducks from a pond pen at a home and carried them away in a crate.", "{DL} believed the ducks were strays at the pond and took them home to look after them."),
        allocution: "\"I thought those eight ducks were strays at the pond, and I took them home to look after them. I've been in this courtroom before for taking chickens, and I should have asked around first. I'll pay for the ducks and for the pen. I'm sorry to the family who owned them.\"",
        truths: ("The pen was latched, and {DL} carried a crate to the pond ready to load the ducks.", "{DL} saw the ducks at the pond and thought they were loose."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take the ducks from the pen?", "\"Yes, I did. I thought they were strays at a pond, and I took them home to look after them.\""), .direct("Why did you think they were strays?", "\"They were at the edge of a pond, and I didn't see a fence at first. I thought someone had abandoned them.\""), .direct("Did you open a latched pen?", "\"I opened a gate on a little pen, and I didn't notice the latch until I was inside. I should have stopped there.\""), .direct("What did you do with the ducks?", "\"I put them in a pen in my yard, gave them food and water, and watched over them. I planned to find the owner.\""), .direct("How did you learn they weren't strays?", "\"The deputies came to my door and told me. I gave them back right away.\""), .direct("What will you do now?", "\"I'll pay for the ducks and for the pen. I'm sorry to the family who owned them.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before for taking chickens, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I should have asked around first. I know how it looks.\""), .cross("You carried a crate to the pond, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I brought it in case I found strays. I know how that looks.\""), .cross("You didn't knock on any door, did you?", "\"No. I should have, and I'm sorry that I didn't.\""), .cross("The pen was latched, wasn't it?", "\"Yes, apparently. I didn't notice at first.\""), .cross("You took all eight ducks, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I wanted to keep them together.\"")],
        openings: ("A homeowner kept eight ducks in a latched pen beside a pond, and the yard camera shows {D} carrying a crate of ducks away. The ducks were worth $200, and {DL} returns to this court having been here in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says {D.he} thought the ducks were strays at the pond, and took them home to look after them. The defense will show an animal lover's mistake, and an owner who has offered to pay for the ducks and the pen."),
        closings: ("The yard camera shows {D} carrying a crate of ducks away from a latched pen. They were worth $200. {DL} came through this court in {PRIORDATE} where the matter was {PRIOR}.", "{D} thought the ducks were strays and meant to look after them. A person who thought the ducks were loose did not mean to take anyone's property. {DL} has offered to pay for the ducks and for the pen."),
        timeline: [(0, "Morning: the homeowner feeds the ducks and latches the pen."), (0, "Afternoon: the yard camera shows {D} carrying a crate toward the pond."), (0, "The homeowner returns, finds the ducks gone and calls deputies.")],
        identified: "Yard Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let photographerDeposit = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.photographerDeposit",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Photographer Takes Wedding Deposit and Never Shows"],
        law: "falsePretenses",
        spec: "Obtained property of {V} by deception, $1,000, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} took a $1,000 deposit for wedding photos and did not appear.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Contract", "A signed contract and receipt.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Illness", "{DL} says {D.he} was ill.")],
        role: "Bride",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about your wedding.", "\"My wedding was on a Saturday afternoon at a garden venue. We'd planned it for a year, with about eighty guests, and photos were important to us.\""), .direct("How did you come to hire {D}?", "\"A friend recommended {DL}. We met, looked at samples and signed a contract for the photos and an album.\""), .direct("How much did you pay?", "\"A $1,000 deposit. I paid by check, and {DL} gave me a signed receipt.\""), .direct("What happened on the day of the wedding?", "\"{DL} never arrived. We waited, my father called, and the calls went to voicemail. We had a friend take pictures on a phone.\""), .direct("What did you do after the wedding?", "\"I called {DL} repeatedly. I got no answer for days, and then I contacted the sheriff's office.\""), .direct("What did it mean to you?", "\"I have no real wedding photos. That was something we can never get back, and I lost the $1,000.\""), .cross("Did {DL} ever contact you afterward?", "\"Eventually, yes, a few days later, with an apology about being sick.\""), .cross("Did {DL} offer to refund the deposit?", "\"{D.He} did, but the money hasn't arrived.\""), .cross("Did {DL} seem reliable when you met?", "\"Yes, {D.he} did, and the samples were good.\""), .cross("Did you see any evidence that {DL} was ill?", "\"I've since heard about a clinic record. I haven't seen it myself.\""), .cross("Did you sign a contract with a cancellation clause?", "\"There was a section about cancellations, but I don't remember the details.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took a $1,000 deposit for wedding photography and never appeared at the wedding.", "{DL} was ill the day of the wedding and could not shoot, though {D.he} failed to call the couple."),
        allocution: "\"I was ill the day of that wedding and couldn't shoot it, and I didn't call the couple. I've been in this courtroom before, and I know that doesn't excuse it. I'll refund the thousand dollars.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} never called the couple, and no photos were ever delivered.", "A clinic record shows {DL} was seen that day, which confirms the illness."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take the $1,000 deposit and miss the wedding?", "\"Yes, I did. I was ill on the wedding day and couldn't work, and I made it worse by not calling.\""), .direct("What was wrong with you?", "\"I had a high fever and a bad stomach illness. I couldn't stand up. I went to a clinic that day.\""), .direct("Why didn't you call the couple?", "\"I was so sick that I didn't think straight, and then I was ashamed. I should have called someone to cover for me.\""), .direct("Do you have proof of the visit?", "\"Yes. A clinic record shows I was seen that day, and I've given it to the deputies.\""), .direct("Why haven't you refunded the deposit?", "\"I spent some of it on supplies and bills. I'm collecting what I need to repay in full.\""), .direct("What will you do now?", "\"I'll refund the $1,000 and apologize to the bride in person.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I know it doesn't excuse what I did.\""), .cross("You never called anyone, did you?", "\"No, I never called anyone, and I should have. Even a short call would have let the couple find another photographer.\""), .cross("You kept the deposit, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I did keep the deposit, and I'll refund every dollar of it as soon as the court allows me to.\""), .cross("The couple had no photos, did they?", "\"No, they had none from a professional, and I'm deeply sorry for that. It's a loss I can't fix by returning money.\""), .cross("You were able to call the clinic, weren't you?", "\"I did, in the morning. I should have called the couple too.\"")],
        openings: ("A bride signed a contract and paid {D} a $1,000 deposit for wedding photos, and {D} never showed up on the wedding day. {D.He} did not call, and {DL} was no stranger to this courtroom after {PRIORDATE} after being charged with {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says {D.he} was ill that day and could not work, and a clinic record shows a visit. The defense will show an illness and a failure to call, not a plan to take the deposit and skip the wedding."),
        closings: ("A bride paid $1,000 for photos, and {D} never appeared and never called. The contract and the receipt are plain. {DL} returns to this court having been here in {PRIORDATE} after being charged with {PRIOR}.", "{DL} was ill on the wedding day, and a clinic record shows it. {D.He} should have called and failed to, and {D.he} will refund the $1,000. That is a failure, but not a deception."),
        timeline: [(-90, "{D} signs a contract and takes a $1,000 deposit from the couple."), (0, "The wedding day: {D} does not appear and does not call."), (3, "The couple tries to reach {D} and reports it to deputies.")],
        identified: "Contract",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let shovelDriveway = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.shovelDriveway",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Neighbor Swings Shovel Over Driveway Dispute"],
        law: "simpleAssault",
        spec: "Assaulted {V} by striking {V.him}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} struck a neighbor with a shovel over a shared driveway.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Street Camera", "{D} swings the shovel.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Line", "{DL} says the driveway was {D.his}.")],
        role: "Neighbor",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about your relationship to {D}.", "\"{DL} is my neighbor. Our homes share a driveway, and we've argued for years over who may park where and where the line is.\""), .direct("What happened that day?", "\"We were shoveling the driveway after a snowstorm, and {DL} told me I was on {D.his} side. We argued, and then {DL} swung a shovel at me.\""), .direct("Where were you struck?", "\"On the upper arm and shoulder. It left a large bruise and I had a cut where the blade caught me.\""), .direct("What does the street camera show?", "\"{DL} swinging the shovel in a wide arc and hitting me. It also shows me with a hand raised.\""), .direct("What did you do after you were struck?", "\"I backed away, called the sheriff and went to urgent care. They told me nothing was broken, but I had stitches.\""), .direct("How has this affected you?", "\"I'm afraid to go outside when {DL} is home. We share a driveway, so I can't avoid {D.him}.\""), .cross("Did you raise your hand before {DL} swung?", "\"I did raise it. I wasn't going to hit {D.him}, but I wanted to stop {D.him}.\""), .cross("Who owns the driveway?", "\"The deed says it's shared. We each have a right to use it.\""), .cross("Have you argued with {DL} about it before?", "\"Yes, many times, including one that nearly came to blows.\""), .cross("Did {DL} apologize?", "\"Yes, a few days later, and I didn't know what to say.\""), .cross("Did you say anything to {DL} before the swing?", "\"I told {D.him} to get off my side. I may have raised my voice.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} struck a neighbor with a shovel during a dispute over a shared driveway.", "{V} raised a hand first, and {DL} swung in the heat of the argument over land {D.he} believed was {D.his}."),
        allocution: "\"We fought over that shared driveway, and I struck my neighbor with a shovel. I've been in this courtroom before for a similar fight. I should have called the sheriff instead of swinging.\"",
        truths: ("The street camera shows {D} swinging the shovel, and the drive is shared by both homes.", "{V} raised a hand toward {D} before the swing."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you strike {V} with the shovel?", "\"Yes, I did. We were arguing over the driveway, and {V.he} raised a hand at me, and I swung without thinking.\""), .direct("Why were you arguing?", "\"I believed the driveway was mine. The survey I saw showed my line running down the middle, and {V} wouldn't move {V.his} car.\""), .direct("What did {V} do before you swung?", "\"{V.He} raised a hand toward my face. I thought {V.he} was about to hit me, and I swung the shovel.\""), .direct("Did you mean to hurt {V}?", "\"I meant to protect myself. I didn't think about what the shovel would do, and I'm sorry that it hit {V.him}.\""), .direct("What did you do afterward?", "\"I dropped the shovel and asked if {V.he} was all right. {V.He} told me to stay away, and I did.\""), .direct("What would you do differently?", "\"I would have called the sheriff instead of swinging, and I would have asked for a survey.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before for a similar fight, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I should have walked away. I'm sorry for losing control.\""), .cross("You swung a shovel at {V.him}, didn't you?", "\"Yes, and I know it could have been much worse.\""), .cross("The deed says the driveway is shared, doesn't it?", "\"Yes, and I should have respected that.\""), .cross("{V} needed stitches, didn't {V.he}?", "\"I've been told so, and I'm sorry.\""), .cross("You could have gone inside, couldn't you?", "\"I could have gone back inside the house and called the sheriff, and I wish I had done that.\"")],
        openings: ("Two neighbors share a driveway, and an argument over where the line runs ended with {D} swinging a shovel at {V}. A street camera caught it, and The court file shows {DL} here in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says the driveway was {D.his}, and {V} raised a hand first. The defense will show an argument that got out of hand, not a plan to hurt anyone."),
        closings: ("The street camera shows {D} swinging a shovel at a neighbor over a shared driveway. A shovel is a dangerous weapon. Court records have {DL} here before, in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}.", "{V} raised a hand first, and {D} reacted in the heat of an old argument. {D.He} is sorry and says {D.he} should have called the sheriff instead of swinging."),
        timeline: [(0, "{D} and {V} argue over the shared driveway."), (0, "{V} raises a hand, and {D} swings the shovel."), (0, "{V} is struck, and a bystander calls deputies.")],
        identified: "Street Camera",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let refundGroceries = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.followup.refundGroceries",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Customer Claims Grocery Orders Never Arrived"],
        law: "falsePretenses",
        spec: "Obtained property of {V} by deception, $520, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} claimed thirty grocery deliveries never arrived and collected $520.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Delivery Records", "Photos show delivered bags.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Stolen", "{DL} says porch pirates took them.")],
        role: "Platform investigator",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about your job.", "\"I'm an investigator for the grocery delivery platform. I review refund claims that look unusual and compare them with delivery photos and driver records.\""), .direct("What caught your attention about {D}'s account?", "\"Thirty refund claims in two months, each saying the groceries never arrived. That is far more than a normal customer files.\""), .direct("What did the delivery records show?", "\"Photos, taken by drivers at the door, showing bags on {DL}'s porch for all of the deliveries I checked.\""), .direct("What did the porch camera show?", "\"{DL} taking bags in from the porch on several of the dates when {D.he} claimed the groceries never arrived.\""), .direct("How much did the platform refund?", "\"A total of $520 across the thirty claims.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I closed the account and referred the case to the sheriff's office with the photos and camera clips.\""), .cross("Did {DL} file a theft report for any of the missing bags?", "\"No. We don't have any record of a report.\""), .cross("Could another person have taken some bags before {DL} came out?", "\"It's possible. Porch theft is common, and I can't rule it out for every delivery.\""), .cross("Did {DL} contact support about the claims?", "\"Yes. {D.He} said the groceries had been stolen, and {D.he} believed it.\""), .cross("Did {DL} offer to repay the platform?", "\"Yes, through a message to our support team.\""), .cross("Do all the camera clips show {DL} taking groceries?", "\"No. Only some of them. The others show nothing either way.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} claimed thirty grocery deliveries never arrived and collected $520 in refunds.", "Porch pirates took the bags, and {DL} believed the claims were honest."),
        allocution: "\"I believed some of those grocery deliveries never arrived, and I claimed refunds without checking with the carrier first. I've been in this courtroom before for a similar claim, and I know how it looks. I'll repay the five hundred twenty dollars. I'm sorry to the store for the confusion.\"",
        truths: ("A porch camera shows {DL} taking the bags inside, and no theft report was ever filed.", "The delivery photos show bags on the porch, which is consistent with someone else taking them first."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you claim thirty deliveries never arrived?", "\"Yes, I did. I believed that porch pirates had taken the bags, and I filed claims without checking with the carrier first.\""), .direct("Why did you believe they were stolen?", "\"Several times, I came home and found nothing on the porch. I'd heard of thefts in my neighborhood, and I assumed it had happened to me.\""), .direct("Did you take bags inside on some of those dates?", "\"Yes, on a few of them. I may have claimed those by mistake when I forgot I'd already brought the groceries in.\""), .direct("Why didn't you file a theft report?", "\"I didn't think of it. I figured the platform would just refund me, and I didn't realize it was an issue.\""), .direct("What did you do with the money?", "\"I spent it on more groceries and on bills. I'll repay all of it.\""), .direct("What will you do now?", "\"I'll repay $520 and check with the carrier before filing any claim.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before for a similar claim, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I can see how it looks to a platform that paid out the money. I should have checked every delivery first.\""), .cross("You filed thirty claims in two months, didn't you?", "\"Yes. It was a lot, and I should have stopped to wonder why.\""), .cross("Photos show bags on your porch, don't they?", "\"Yes, and I didn't check them.\""), .cross("You never called the carrier, did you?", "\"No, I didn't. I never called the carrier about it.\""), .cross("You received $520, didn't you?", "\"Yes, and I'll repay it.\"")],
        openings: ("A grocery delivery platform paid out $520 in refunds after {D} claimed thirty deliveries never arrived. Delivery photos show bags left on the porch, and The court file shows {DL} here in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says porch pirates took the bags, and {D.he} claimed refunds in good faith. The defense will show that {D.he} did not know the carrier left the bags, and that {D.he} has offered to repay the platform."),
        closings: ("The platform's photos show thirty deliveries left on {D}'s porch, and {D} claimed none arrived. A porch camera shows {D.him} taking the bags inside. {DL} stood in this court once before, in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}.", "{DL} believed the bags were stolen and filed claims in good faith. {D} has offered to repay the $520, and the State has not shown that {D.he} knew the groceries had been delivered."),
